</span></td></tr>
<tr id="Sx1.T1.2.16" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="Sx1.T1.2.16.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.16.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.16.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Sx1.T1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{ab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{ab}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="Sx1.T1.2.16.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.16.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:142.3pt;">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.16.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Cost of predicting class <math id="Sx1.T1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> when true class is <math id="Sx1.T1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="Sx1.T1.2.17" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="Sx1.T1.2.17.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.17.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.17.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Sx1.T1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}_{R}\subseteq\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}_{R}\subseteq\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="Sx1.T1.2.17.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.17.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:142.3pt;">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.17.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Set of rare, high‑impact classes</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="Sx1.T1.2.18" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="Sx1.T1.2.18.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.18.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.18.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Sx1.T1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P,h)=e_{\tau}(C_{h(P^{\top}X),Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P,h)=e_{\tau}(C_{h(P^{\top}X),Y})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="Sx1.T1.2.18.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.18.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:142.3pt;">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.18.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">represent the joint risk objective function of exp2PCA.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="Sx1.T1.2.19" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="Sx1.T1.2.19.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.19.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.19.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Sx1.T1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="Sx1.T1.2.19.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.19.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:142.3pt;">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.19.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Expectile parameter (<math id="Sx1.T1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\to 1^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\to 1^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> targets extreme tails)</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="Sx1.T1.2.20" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="Sx1.T1.2.20.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.20.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.20.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Sx1.T1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="Sx1.T1.2.20.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.20.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:142.3pt;">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.20.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Risk‑weighted covariance matrix used in ExPCA</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="Sx1.T1.2.21" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="Sx1.T1.2.21.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.21.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.21.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Sx1.T1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\esssup(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ess</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>sup</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\esssup(L)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="Sx1.T1.2.21.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_r">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.21.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:142.3pt;">
<span id="Sx1.T1.2.21.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Essential supremum of random variable <math id="Sx1.T1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">II </span><span id="S2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Problem Formulation</span></h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\mathbb{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\mathbb{P})</annotation></semantics></math> be a complete probability space. Let <math id="S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a square-integrable random vector with mean vector <math id="S2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\mathbb{E}[X]\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\mathbb{E}[X]\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and a symmetric, trace-class covariance matrix <math id="S2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\mathbb{E}[(X-\mu)(X-\mu)^{\top}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\mathbb{E}[(X-\mu)(X-\mu)^{\top}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the spectral theorem for symmetric compact operators, the orthogonal decomposition of <math id="S2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\sum_{j=1}^{d}\lambda_{j}v_{j}v_{j}^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\sum_{j=1}^{d}\lambda_{j}v_{j}v_{j}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the eigenvalues are sorted as <math id="S2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}\geq\lambda_{2}\geq\dots\geq\lambda_{d}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}\geq\lambda_{2}\geq\dots\geq\lambda_{d}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{j}\}_{j=1}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{j}\}_{j=1}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> forms an orthonormal basis of <math id="S2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a user-defined retained-variance threshold <math id="S2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the target truncation rank <math id="S2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\{1,\dots,d-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\{1,\dots,d-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniquely determined by:</p>
<table id="S2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=\min\left\{m\in\{1,\dots,d\}:\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{m}\lambda_{j}}{\sum_{j=1}^{d}\lambda_{j}}\geq\rho\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=\min\left\{m\in\{1,\dots,d\}:\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{m}\lambda_{j}}{\sum_{j=1}^{d}\lambda_{j}}\geq\rho\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{r}=\{P\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times r}:P^{\top}P=I_{r}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{r}=\{P\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times r}:P^{\top}P=I_{r}\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the Stiefel manifold of semi-orthogonal matrices. The canonical semi-orthogonal matrix aligned with the dominant variance is <math id="S2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{r}=[v_{1},\dots,v_{r}]\in\mathcal{U}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{r}=[v_{1},\dots,v_{r}]\in\mathcal{U}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. The corresponding orthogonal projection operator on <math id="S2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as <math id="S2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}=P_{r}P_{r}^{\top}=\sum_{j=1}^{r}v_{j}v_{j}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}=P_{r}P_{r}^{\top}=\sum_{j=1}^{r}v_{j}v_{j}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, and its orthogonal complement operator is <math id="S2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}^{\perp}=I_{d}-\Pi_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}^{\perp}=I_{d}-\Pi_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The classical principal component representation is the compressed random vector <math id="S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{r}=P_{r}^{\top}X\in\mathbb{R}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{r}=P_{r}^{\top}X\in\mathbb{R}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. The discarded noise subspace is explicitly designated as <math id="S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{R}=\Span\{v_{r+1},\dots,v_{d}\}=\text{Im}(\Pi_{r}^{\perp})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>span</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Im</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{R}=\Span\{v_{r+1},\dots,v_{d}\}=\text{Im}(\Pi_{r}^{\perp})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">II-A</span> </span><span id="S2.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Latent-Factor Model</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We assume that the observable data satisfies a structural latent-factor representation:</p>
<table id="S2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\mu+\sum_{j=1}^{d}z_{j}v_{j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\mu+\sum_{j=1}^{d}z_{j}v_{j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the latent coordinates <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{j}=v_{j}^{\top}(X-\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{j}=v_{j}^{\top}(X-\mu)</annotation></semantics></math> are mutually independent, centered random variables satisfying <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[z_{j}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[z_{j}]=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[z_{j}^{2}]=\lambda_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[z_{j}^{2}]=\lambda_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. No parametric distributional assumptions (e.g., joint Gaussianity) are imposed on these factors.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\in\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\in\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math> represent a categorical class label generated via a deterministic, Borel-measurable mapping:</p>
<table id="S2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=g\bigl(\{z_{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{M}}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=g\bigl(\{z_{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{M}}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}\subseteq\{r+1,\dots,d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}\subseteq\{r+1,\dots,d\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a non-empty index set. Under this setting, <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> is conditionally independent of the principal subspace given the discarded coordinates; thus, the descriptive information regarding <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> resides exclusively within the minor subspace <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. This represents the absolute worst-case configuration for variance-maximization paradigms, typically modeling regimes where rare, high-stakes events are structurally masked by heavy background noise.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">II-B</span> </span><span id="S2.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Dimensionality Reduction and Decision-Theoretic Frameworks</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To formalize paradigms that extract information from <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, we introduce the functional definitions of statistical expectiles, followed by the formulations of traditional, robust, and our proposed decision-directed dimensionality reduction methods.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">II-B</span>1 </span>The Expectile Functional</h4>

<div id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Before evaluating subspace models, we define the asymmetric tail-risk operator used throughout this work.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Expectile of a Random Variable)<span id="Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\in L^{2}(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\mathbb{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\in L^{2}(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\mathbb{P})</annotation></semantics></math> be a square-integrable scalar random variable. For an asymmetry tail parameter <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-expectile functional <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\tau}(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\tau}(W)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as the unique minimizer of an asymmetrically weighted quadratic loss:</p>
<table id="S2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\tau}(W)=\arg\min_{t\in\mathcal{R}}\mathbb{E}\bigl[\ell_{\tau}(W-t)\bigr]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\tau}(W)=\arg\min_{t\in\mathcal{R}}\mathbb{E}\bigl[\ell_{\tau}(W-t)\bigr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the loss function <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\tau}(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\tau}(u)</annotation></semantics></math> is parameterized by:</p>
<table id="S2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\ell_{\tau}(u)=\left|\tau-\mathbf{1}_{\{u&lt;0\}}\right|u^{2}=\begin{cases}\tau u^{2}&amp;\text{if }u\geq 0,\\
(1-\tau)u^{2}&amp;\text{if }u&lt;0.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\tau}(u)=\left|\tau-\mathbf{1}_{\{u&lt;0\}}\right|u^{2}=\begin{cases}\tau u^{2}&amp;\text{if }u\geq 0,\\
(1-\tau)u^{2}&amp;\text{if }u&lt;0.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 1</span></span><span id="Thmremark1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As the parameter tracks the extreme upper tail (<math id="Thmremark1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\to 1</annotation></semantics></math>), the expectile functional <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\tau}(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\tau}(W)</annotation></semantics></math> converges asymptotically to the essential supremum of the random variable’s distribution (<math id="Thmremark1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ess\,sup}\,W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>ess sup</mtext><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ess\,sup}\,W</annotation></semantics></math>). This property renders it a highly coherent, non-linear index of worst-case risk exposure. See <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite> for details.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">II-B</span>2 </span>Unsupervised Subspace Paradigms</h4>

<div id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider an arbitrary compression matrix <math id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in\mathcal{U}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in\mathcal{U}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> mapping to a low-dimensional coordinate representation <math id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=P^{\top}X\in\mathbb{R}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=P^{\top}X\in\mathbb{R}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. The geometric reconstruction of <math id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> within the original space is given by <math id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}=PZ=PP^{\top}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}=PZ=PP^{\top}X</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Standard Unsupervised PCA)<span id="Thmdefinition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Standard PCA identifies a rank-<math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> subspace that minimizes the expected <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> reconstruction error:</p>
<table id="S2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{PCA}}=\arg\min_{P\in\mathcal{U}_{r}}\mathbb{E}\left\|X-PP^{\top}X\right\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{PCA}}=\arg\min_{P\in\mathcal{U}_{r}}\mathbb{E}\left\|X-PP^{\top}X\right\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By the Eckart–Young–Mirsky theorem, the optimal solution <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{PCA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{PCA}}</annotation></semantics></math> is spanned precisely by the <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> leading eigenvectors <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{r}=[v_{1},\dots,v_{r}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{r}=[v_{1},\dots,v_{r}]</annotation></semantics></math> of the covariance matrix <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Tail-Preserving PCA (TP-PCA))<span id="Thmdefinition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given i.i.d. data <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(X_{i},Y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(X_{i},Y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}_{R}\subset\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}_{R}\subset\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of rare, high-impact classes (e.g., fraud, disease). Define weights <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w_{i}=1+\alpha\mathbf{1}_{\{Y_{i}\in\mathcal{Y}_{R}\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}=1+\alpha\mathbf{1}_{\{Y_{i}\in\mathcal{Y}_{R}\}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. We compute weighted mean <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{w}=(\sum_{i=1}^{n}w_{i}X_{i})/(\sum_{j=1}^{n}w_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{w}=(\sum_{i=1}^{n}w_{i}X_{i})/(\sum_{j=1}^{n}w_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> and weighted covariance <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{w}=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{n}w_{i}(X_{i}-\mu_{w})(X_{i}-\mu_{w})^{\top}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}w_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{w}=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{n}w_{i}(X_{i}-\mu_{w})(X_{i}-\mu_{w})^{\top}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}w_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>. TP-PCA projects onto the top <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> eigenvectors of <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>. This amplifies the influence of rare-event samples.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Expectile PCA / exPCA)<span id="Thmdefinition4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Expectile PCA incorporates geometric tail-awareness by minimizing the <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-expectile of the squared Euclidean reconstruction error distribution:</p>
<table id="S2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{exPCA}}=\arg\min_{P\in\mathcal{U}_{r}}e_{\tau}\left(\left\|X-PP^{\top}X\right\|^{2}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>exPCA</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{exPCA}}=\arg\min_{P\in\mathcal{U}_{r}}e_{\tau}\left(\left\|X-PP^{\top}X\right\|^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">exPCA prioritizes finding directions that robustly bound the worst-case geometric reconstruction distortions for outlying data vectors.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS3.6" class="ltx_text">II-B</span>3 </span>Supervised Subspace Paradigm: exp2PCA</h4>

<div id="S2.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To couple dimensionality reduction directly with a downstream operational task, we formalize the decision-theoretic risk space. Let <math id="S2.SS2.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}^{K\times K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}^{K\times K}</annotation></semantics></math> be an asymmetric misclassification cost matrix satisfying <math id="S2.SS2.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{aa}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{aa}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{a\neq b}C_{ab}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{a\neq b}C_{ab}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S2.SS2.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\in\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\in\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S2.SS2.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}=\{h:\mathbb{R}^{r}\to\{1,\dots,K\}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}=\{h:\mathbb{R}^{r}\to\{1,\dots,K\}\}</annotation></semantics></math> define the class of Borel-measurable operational classifiers acting on the compressed space.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given a choice of embedding matrix <math id="S2.SS2.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in\mathcal{U}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in\mathcal{U}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and a classifier <math id="S2.SS2.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, the decision loss is a discrete random variable <math id="S2.SS2.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(P,h)=C_{h(P^{\top}X),Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(P,h)=C_{h(P^{\top}X),Y}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 5</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Expectile Misclassification Cost PCA / exp2PCA)<span id="Thmdefinition5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The exp2PCA framework defines the optimal rank-<math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> representation as the joint minimizer of the <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-expectile of the downstream classification cost:</p>
<table id="S2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{\text{exp2}},h_{\text{exp2}})=\arg\min_{P\in\mathcal{U}_{r},\,h\in\mathcal{H}}e_{\tau}\big(C_{h(P^{\top}X),Y}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>exp2</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>exp2</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{\text{exp2}},h_{\text{exp2}})=\arg\min_{P\in\mathcal{U}_{r},\,h\in\mathcal{H}}e_{\tau}\big(C_{h(P^{\top}X),Y}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">By substituting geometric reconstruction criteria with a direct minimization of the decision penalty’s tail risk, exp2PCA explicitly preserves crucial classification signals, even when they reside entirely along the minor principal components of the data vector.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">II-C</span> </span><span id="S2.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fundamental Limits of PCA for Rare-Event Classification</span></h3>

<section id="S2.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">II-C</span>1 </span>Complete Information Erasure</h4>

<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Information Erasure)<span id="Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the structural latent-mapping factor model where <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=g(\{z_{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=g(\{z_{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}\subseteq\{r+1,\dots,d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}\subseteq\{r+1,\dots,d\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the following statements hold true:</span></p>
<ol id="S2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\perp\!\!\!\perp P_{r}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mpadded style="width:0.518em;" width="0.518em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\perp\!\!\!\perp P_{r}X</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The mutual information vanishes: </span><math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Y;P_{r}X)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;P_{r}X)=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(Y=k\mid P_{r}X)=\mathbb{P}(Y=k)=\pi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(Y=k\mid P_{r}X)=\mathbb{P}(Y=k)=\pi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> a.s. for every category </span><math id="S2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS1.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Observe that the PCA reconstruction can be explicitly written as <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{r}X=P_{r}\mu+\sum_{j=1}^{r}z_{j}v_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{r}X=P_{r}\mu+\sum_{j=1}^{r}z_{j}v_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. The generated sub-<math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra satisfies <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(P_{r}X)\subseteq\sigma(z_{1},\dots,z_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(P_{r}X)\subseteq\sigma(z_{1},\dots,z_{r})</annotation></semantics></math>. By the model construction, the label <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra satisfies <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(Y)\subseteq\sigma(\{z_{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(Y)\subseteq\sigma(\{z_{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}\cap\{1,\dots,r\}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}\cap\{1,\dots,r\}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>, the mutual independence of the complete latent coordinate set <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{z_{j}\}_{j=1}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{z_{j}\}_{j=1}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> implies that <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(z_{1},\dots,z_{r})\perp\!\!\!\perp\sigma(\{z_{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.518em;" width="0.518em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(z_{1},\dots,z_{r})\perp\!\!\!\perp\sigma(\{z_{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows directly that <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\perp\!\!\!\perp P_{r}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mpadded style="width:0.518em;" width="0.518em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\perp\!\!\!\perp P_{r}X</annotation></semantics></math>. Statements (2) and (3) are immediate structural consequences of this independence.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">II-C</span>2 </span>Bayes Expected Cost Collapse</h4>

<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Bayes Collapse)<span id="Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}=\mathbb{P}(Y=k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}=\mathbb{P}(Y=k)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the prior class probabilities. For any measurable classifier <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{r}\to\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{r}\to\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math> operating on the standard PCA projection space, the infimum expected cost collapses:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{f}\mathbb{E}\bigl[C_{f(P_{r}X),Y}\bigr]=\min_{a\in\{1,\dots,K\}}\sum_{b=1}^{K}C_{ab}\pi_{b}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mi>f</mi></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{f}\mathbb{E}\bigl[C_{f(P_{r}X),Y}\bigr]=\min_{a\in\{1,\dots,K\}}\sum_{b=1}^{K}C_{ab}\pi_{b}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This lower bound is achieved identically by a constant classifier <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(X)\equiv a^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(X)\equiv a^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, PCA compression provides zero decision-theoretic utility over completely ignoring the data vector.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the law of total expectation and leveraging the conditional independence from Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Information Erasure). ‣ II-C1 Complete Information Erasure ‣ II-C Fundamental Limits of PCA for Rare-Event Classification ‣ II Problem Formulation ‣ The Risk Shadow of Principal Component Analysis: When 99.9999% Variance Preservation Causes Catastrophic Decision Errors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we can decompose the expected cost objective function as:</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[C_{f(P_{r}X),Y}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[C_{f(P_{r}X),Y}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\mathbb{E}\bigl[C_{f(P_{r}X),Y}\mid P_{r}X\bigr]\Bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\mathbb{E}\bigl[C_{f(P_{r}X),Y}\mid P_{r}X\bigr]\Bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{b=1}^{K}C_{f(P_{r}X),b}\,\mathbb{P}(Y=b\mid P_{r}X)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{b=1}^{K}C_{f(P_{r}X),b}\,\mathbb{P}(Y=b\mid P_{r}X)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{b=1}^{K}C_{f(P_{r}X),b}\,\pi_{b}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{b=1}^{K}C_{f(P_{r}X),b}\,\pi_{b}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">To minimize this expectation point-wise for any realization of <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{r}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{r}X</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal action is to choose the constant category index <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{*}\in\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{*}\in\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math> that minimizes the deterministic prior cost vector assignment:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{*}\in\arg\min_{a\in\{1,\dots,K\}}\sum_{b=1}^{K}C_{ab}\pi_{b}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{*}\in\arg\min_{a\in\{1,\dots,K\}}\sum_{b=1}^{K}C_{ab}\pi_{b}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is entirely decoupled from the realization of <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{r}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{r}X</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal function <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> collapses to a constant allocation mapping, completing the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS4.6" class="ltx_text">II-D</span> </span><span id="S2.SS4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Risk Shadow</span></h3>

<div id="Thmdefinition6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 6</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Risk Shadow)<span id="Thmdefinition6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A representation <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi(X)</annotation></semantics></math> induces a <em id="Thmdefinition6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Risk Shadow</em> if <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Y;\Psi(X))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;\Psi(X))=0</annotation></semantics></math> yet the nominal accuracy (or average cost) can be made arbitrarily close to optimal by a constant predictor, while the tail risk remains unbounded.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(PCA-Induced Risk Shadow)<span id="Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the latent-factor model with <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}\subseteq\{r+1,\dots,d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}\subseteq\{r+1,\dots,d\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the PCA representation <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{r}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{r}X</annotation></semantics></math> induces a Risk Shadow. Moreover, for any <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> there exists a prior distribution with a dominating class such that the constant classifier achieves accuracy <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;1-\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;1-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> while <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Y;P_{r}X)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;P_{r}X)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS4.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Information erasure gives <math id="S2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Take <math id="S2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{a_{0}}&gt;1-\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{a_{0}}&gt;1-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>; then constant classifier predicting <math id="S2.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> has accuracy <math id="S2.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;1-\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;1-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. The tail risk (e.g., expectile at <math id="S2.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> close to 1) is determined by the rare classes and is unaffected by the constant classifier’s high accuracy. Hence the shadow exists.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS5.6" class="ltx_text">II-E</span> </span><span id="S2.SS5.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Risk-Aware Unsupervised Dimensionality Reduction: exPCA</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To systematically protect against worst-case structural failures, we formalize the stationarity conditions and information-theoretic behavior of Expectile PCA (exPCA) under extreme tail parameters (<math id="S2.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\to 1^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\to 1^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>). Let <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}(d,r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}(d,r)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the Grassmannian manifold of all <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional linear subspaces in <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. For an orthogonal embedding matrix <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in\mathcal{U}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in\mathcal{U}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{P}(X)=\|X-PP^{\top}X\|^{2}=\|(I_{d}-PP^{\top})X\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{P}(X)=\|X-PP^{\top}X\|^{2}=\|(I_{d}-PP^{\top})X\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the quadratic reconstruction error random variable.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Weighted Covariance Characterization)<span id="Thmproposition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{r}^{(\tau)}\in\mathcal{U}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{r}^{(\tau)}\in\mathcal{U}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> be a stationary point of the exPCA objective function. Define the asymmetric indicator weight function <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\tau}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathcal{U}_{r}\to\mathbb{R}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\tau}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathcal{U}_{r}\to\mathbb{R}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> by:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w_{\tau}(X;P)=\tau\mathbf{1}_{\{R_{P}(X)\geq e_{\tau}(R_{P})\}}+(1-\tau)\mathbf{1}_{\{R_{P}(X)&lt;e_{\tau}(R_{P})\}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>e</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>e</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\tau}(X;P)=\tau\mathbf{1}_{\{R_{P}(X)\geq e_{\tau}(R_{P})\}}+(1-\tau)\mathbf{1}_{\{R_{P}(X)&lt;e_{\tau}(R_{P})\}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, the subspace spanned by the columns of <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{r}^{(\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{r}^{(\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math> is invariant under the weighted raw second-moment matrix <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\tau}=\mathbb{E}\left[w_{\tau}(X;P_{r}^{(\tau)})XX^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\tau}=\mathbb{E}\left[w_{\tau}(X;P_{r}^{(\tau)})XX^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>. That is, <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{r}^{(\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{r}^{(\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math> maps onto the <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional dominant eigenspace of <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition, for a fixed <math id="S2.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, the scalar <math id="S2.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-expectile <math id="S2.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e=e_{\tau}(R_{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e=e_{\tau}(R_{P})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the first-order optimization condition:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[|\tau-\mathbf{1}_{\{R_{P}(X)&lt;e\}}|(R_{P}(X)-e)\bigr]=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[|\tau-\mathbf{1}_{\{R_{P}(X)&lt;e\}}|(R_{P}(X)-e)\bigr]=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">which can be compactly expressed as <math id="S2.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[w_{\tau}(X;P)(R_{P}(X)-e)]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[w_{\tau}(X;P)(R_{P}(X)-e)]=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, consider the joint objective function mapped onto the Grassmannian manifold, <math id="S2.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(P)=\mathbb{E}\left[w_{\tau}(X;P)(R_{P}(X)-e_{\tau}(R_{P}))^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(P)=\mathbb{E}\left[w_{\tau}(X;P)(R_{P}(X)-e_{\tau}(R_{P}))^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S2.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> represent an infinitesimal variation of <math id="S2.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> constrained to the tangent space of the Stiefel manifold <math id="S2.SS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, enforcing the orthogonality condition <math id="S2.SS5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{\top}P+P^{\top}\delta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{\top}P+P^{\top}\delta=0</annotation></semantics></math>. By the envelope theorem, the implicit derivative of <math id="S2.SS5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(P)</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="S2.SS5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\tau}(R_{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\tau}(R_{P})</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes identically via (<a href="#S2.E16" title="In Proof. ‣ II-E Risk-Aware Unsupervised Dimensionality Reduction: exPCA ‣ II Problem Formulation ‣ The Risk Shadow of Principal Component Analysis: When 99.9999% Variance Preservation Causes Catastrophic Decision Errors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>). Taking the variation of <math id="S2.SS5.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(P)</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="S2.SS5.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> yields:</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta F(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta F(P)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[w_{\tau}(X;P)\cdot\delta\|(I_{d}-PP^{\top})X\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[w_{\tau}(X;P)\cdot\delta\|(I_{d}-PP^{\top})X\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-4\,\mathbb{E}\left[w_{\tau}(X;P)\cdot\text{Tr}\left(\delta^{\top}XX^{\top}P\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>Tr</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-4\,\mathbb{E}\left[w_{\tau}(X;P)\cdot\text{Tr}\left(\delta^{\top}XX^{\top}P\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-4\,\text{Tr}\left(\delta^{\top}\mathbb{E}\left[w_{\tau}(X;P)XX^{\top}\right]P\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-4\,\text{Tr}\left(\delta^{\top}\mathbb{E}\left[w_{\tau}(X;P)XX^{\top}\right]P\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Setting the directional derivative to zero for all admissible variations <math id="S2.SS5.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> on the manifold yields the necessary geometric stationarity condition:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\tau}P=P\left(P^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}P\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\tau}P=P\left(P^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}P\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Multiplying from the left by <math id="S2.SS5.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I_{d}-PP^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I_{d}-PP^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math> yields <math id="S2.SS5.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I_{d}-PP^{\top})\Sigma_{\tau}P=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I_{d}-PP^{\top})\Sigma_{\tau}P=0</annotation></semantics></math>, which states that the subspace <math id="S2.SS5.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Im}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Im</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Im}(P)</annotation></semantics></math> is an invariant subspace of <math id="S2.SS5.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>. Ordering the eigenvalues forces <math id="S2.SS5.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{r}^{(\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{r}^{(\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math> to span the <math id="S2.SS5.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> leading eigenvectors of <math id="S2.SS5.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 2</span></span><span id="Thmremark2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Fixed-Point Algorithmic Scheme)<span id="Thmremark2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Weighted Covariance Characterization). ‣ II-E Risk-Aware Unsupervised Dimensionality Reduction: exPCA ‣ II Problem Formulation ‣ The Risk Shadow of Principal Component Analysis: When 99.9999% Variance Preservation Causes Catastrophic Decision Errors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> naturally yields an Iterative Reweighted Principal Component Analysis (IR-PCA) algorithm. Given an estimate <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> at iteration <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ol id="S2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Compute empirical reconstruction residuals: <math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}^{(k)}=\|(I_{d}-P^{(k)}(P^{(k)})^{\top})X_{i}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}^{(k)}=\|(I_{d}-P^{(k)}(P^{(k)})^{\top})X_{i}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Determine <math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\tau}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\tau}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> by computing the scalar <math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-expectile of <math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{R_{i}^{(k)}\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{R_{i}^{(k)}\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Evaluate sample weights: <math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w_{i}^{(k)}=\tau\mathbf{1}_{\{R_{i}^{(k)}\geq e_{\tau}^{(k)}\}}+(1-\tau)\mathbf{1}_{\{R_{i}^{(k)}&lt;e_{\tau}^{(k)}\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>e</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>e</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}^{(k)}=\tau\mathbf{1}_{\{R_{i}^{(k)}\geq e_{\tau}^{(k)}\}}+(1-\tau)\mathbf{1}_{\{R_{i}^{(k)}&lt;e_{\tau}^{(k)}\}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Construct the empirical weighted matrix: <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{w}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}w_{i}^{(k)}X_{i}X_{i}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{w}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}w_{i}^{(k)}X_{i}X_{i}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Update <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{(k+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{(k+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> via the <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> leading eigenvectors of <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="Thmremark2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Under standard compactness assumptions on the constraint manifold, the objective decreases monotonically, ensuring convergence toward a valid stationary point.</p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">II-E</span>1 </span>Information Re-allocation Properties of exPCA</h4>

<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now prove that exPCA successfully redirects information-theoretic resource allocation to the minor components under high tail-weights (<math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\to 1^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\to 1^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(exPCA Strictly Outperforms PCA)<span id="Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the generative latent-factor model where the categorical label satisfies <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=g(\{z_{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=g(\{z_{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> for a non-empty index set <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}\subseteq\{r+1,\dots,d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}\subseteq\{r+1,\dots,d\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{r}^{\text{PCA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">PCA</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{r}^{\text{PCA}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the standard PCA projection matrix and <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{r}^{(\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{r}^{(\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the exPCA matrix under tail parameter <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then:</span></p>
<ol id="S2.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The classical PCA mutual information is erased: </span><math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Y;P_{r}^{\text{PCA}}X)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">PCA</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;P_{r}^{\text{PCA}}X)=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under an extreme upper tail weight, the mutual information is strictly positive:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\tau\to 1^{-}}I(Y;P_{r}^{(\tau)}X)&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\tau\to 1^{-}}I(Y;P_{r}^{(\tau)}X)&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For a sufficiently high tail parameter <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, exPCA retains strictly more information regarding the rare-event dynamics than standard PCA.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The first assertion follows directly from Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Information Erasure). ‣ II-C1 Complete Information Erasure ‣ II-C Fundamental Limits of PCA for Rare-Event Classification ‣ II Problem Formulation ‣ The Risk Shadow of Principal Component Analysis: When 99.9999% Variance Preservation Causes Catastrophic Decision Errors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. To establish the second assertion, observe that as <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\to 1^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\to 1^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>, the expectile boundary converges to the essential supremum: <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\tau}(R_{P})\to\text{ess\,sup}\,R_{P}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mtext>ess sup</mtext><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\tau}(R_{P})\to\text{ess\,sup}\,R_{P}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose by contradiction that <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\tau\to 1^{-}}P_{r}^{(\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\tau\to 1^{-}}P_{r}^{(\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math> retains a configuration orthogonal to the discriminative subspace <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\mathcal{M}}=\Span\{v_{j}:j\in\mathcal{M}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>span</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\mathcal{M}}=\Span\{v_{j}:j\in\mathcal{M}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under this assumption, for any sample drawn from the rare event configuration (<math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=m</annotation></semantics></math>), its coordinates along <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> are non-zero. Since these coordinates are discarded by the projection, they map directly into the reconstruction error:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{P}(X)\geq\sum_{j\in\mathcal{M}}z_{j}^{2}&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{P}(X)\geq\sum_{j\in\mathcal{M}}z_{j}^{2}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Because the background majority distribution is centered and independent, the maximum possible reconstruction errors are driven strictly by these unaligned, highly dispersed rare states. Thus, as <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\to 1^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\to 1^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>, the indicator function isolates this boundary, and the weight function transforms into a Radon-Nikodym derivative that concentrates all probability mass onto the rare-event support set <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}=\{X:Y\in\mathcal{M}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}=\{X:Y\in\mathcal{M}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The asymptotic weighted covariance matrix converges in operator norm to the conditional expectation:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\tau\to 1^{-}}\Sigma_{\tau}=\mathbb{E}\left[XX^{\top}\;\middle|\;X\in\mathcal{E}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></munder><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\tau\to 1^{-}}\Sigma_{\tau}=\mathbb{E}\left[XX^{\top}\;\middle|\;X\in\mathcal{E}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the mutual independence of the latent coordinates, the conditional variance along the minor axes is strictly positive: <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[z_{j}^{2}\mid X\in\mathcal{E}]=\sigma_{j}^{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[z_{j}^{2}\mid X\in\mathcal{E}]=\sigma_{j}^{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\tau\to 1^{-}}\Sigma_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\tau\to 1^{-}}\Sigma_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> develops dominant directional eigenvalues along <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{r}^{(\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{r}^{(\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math> resolves the dominant eigenspace of <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> by Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Weighted Covariance Characterization). ‣ II-E Risk-Aware Unsupervised Dimensionality Reduction: exPCA ‣ II Problem Formulation ‣ The Risk Shadow of Principal Component Analysis: When 99.9999% Variance Preservation Causes Catastrophic Decision Errors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the columns of <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\tau\to 1^{-}}P_{r}^{(\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\tau\to 1^{-}}P_{r}^{(\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math> must intersect non-trivially with <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This introduces a non-trivial dependency between the compressed random vector <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=(P_{r}^{(\tau)})^{\top}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=(P_{r}^{(\tau)})^{\top}X</annotation></semantics></math> and the category variable <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>, ensuring that the conditional distribution <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(Y\mid P_{r}^{(\tau)}X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(Y\mid P_{r}^{(\tau)}X)</annotation></semantics></math> deviates from the prior distribution. By the continuous mapping theorem applied to the relative entropy functional, it follows that <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\tau\to 1^{-}}I(Y;P_{r}^{(\tau)}X)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\tau\to 1^{-}}I(Y;P_{r}^{(\tau)}X)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS6.6" class="ltx_text">II-F</span> </span><span id="S2.SS6.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Geometric Subspace Misalignment Analysis</span></h3>

<div id="Thmdefinition7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 7</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Principal Angles and Grassmann Distance)<span id="Thmdefinition7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d,r\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d,r\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq r\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq r\leq d</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U,V\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U,V\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> be two matrices with orthonormal columns, satisfying <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\top}U=V^{\top}V=I_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\top}U=V^{\top}V=I_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, whose columns span two <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional linear subspaces <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}=\operatorname{span}(U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>span</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}=\operatorname{span}(U)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}=\operatorname{span}(V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>span</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}=\operatorname{span}(V)</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. The principal angles <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\theta_{1}\leq\theta_{2}\leq\cdots\leq\theta_{r}\leq\frac{\pi}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\theta_{1}\leq\theta_{2}\leq\cdots\leq\theta_{r}\leq\frac{\pi}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> between the subspaces <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> are uniquely defined through the singular values of the matrix product <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\top}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\top}V</annotation></semantics></math>, arranged in descending order:
<math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}(U^{\top}V)=\cos(\theta_{i}),\qquad\forall i\in\{1,\ldots,r\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}(U^{\top}V)=\cos(\theta_{i}),\qquad\forall i\in\{1,\ldots,r\}.</annotation></semantics></math>
The unique orthogonal projection operators onto the subspaces <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> are given respectively by the symmetric, idempotent matrices:
<math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{U}:=UU^{\top},\qquad\Pi_{V}:=VV^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{U}:=UU^{\top},\qquad\Pi_{V}:=VV^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math>
The Grassmannian distance <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}(U,V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}(U,V)</annotation></semantics></math> between the two subspaces is defined via the Frobenius norm of the difference between their orthogonal projectors:
<math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}(U,V):=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\|\Pi_{U}-\Pi_{V}\|_{F}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}(U,V):=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\|\Pi_{U}-\Pi_{V}\|_{F},</annotation></semantics></math>
which satisfies the exact geometric identity:
<math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}^{2}(U,V)=\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sin^{2}(\theta_{i})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}^{2}(U,V)=\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sin^{2}(\theta_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Risk-Induced Rotation of Principal Subspaces)<span id="Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a random vector with a well-defined symmetric, positive semi-definite covariance operator <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\mathbb{E}[(X-\mathbb{E}[X])(X-\mathbb{E}[X])^{\top}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\mathbb{E}[(X-\mathbb{E}[X])(X-\mathbb{E}[X])^{\top}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let the spectral decomposition of <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> be given by:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\lambda_{i}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\lambda_{i}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the eigenvalues are ordered as <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}\geq\lambda_{2}\geq\cdots\geq\lambda_{d}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}\geq\lambda_{2}\geq\cdots\geq\lambda_{d}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{u_{i}\}_{i=1}^{d}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u_{i}\}_{i=1}^{d}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> forms an orthonormal basis of eigenvectors.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a target dimension <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\{1,\ldots,d-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\{1,\ldots,d-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the baseline <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional PCA subspace by the matrix <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{r}=[u_{1},\ldots,u_{r}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{r}=[u_{1},\ldots,u_{r}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> and its corresponding orthogonal projector <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}:=U_{r}U_{r}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}:=U_{r}U_{r}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume the strict spectral separation condition holds at index <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{r}:=\lambda_{r}-\lambda_{r+1}&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{r}:=\lambda_{r}-\lambda_{r+1}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> parameterize an expectile weighting function <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\tau}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\tau}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>, and define the exPCA covariance operator <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\tau}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\tau}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> as the symmetric perturbation:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\tau}=\Sigma+\Delta_{\tau},\quad\text{where}\quad\Delta_{\tau}:=\mathbb{E}\left[\bigl(w_{\tau}(X)-1\bigr)XX^{\top}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\tau}=\Sigma+\Delta_{\tau},\quad\text{where}\quad\Delta_{\tau}:=\mathbb{E}\left[\bigl(w_{\tau}(X)-1\bigr)XX^{\top}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|</annotation></semantics></math> denote the spectral operator norm. Provided <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta_{\tau}\|&lt;\frac{\delta_{r}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta_{\tau}\|&lt;\frac{\delta_{r}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the perturbed operator <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> possesses a unique, isolated, dominant <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional invariant eigenspace <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{r}^{(\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{r}^{(\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math> associated with its <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> largest eigenvalues. Let <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{r}^{(\tau)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{r}^{(\tau)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> denote any matrix with orthonormal columns spanning <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{r}^{(\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{r}^{(\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}:=U_{r}^{(\tau)}(U_{r}^{(\tau)})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}:=U_{r}^{(\tau)}(U_{r}^{(\tau)})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> be its unique orthogonal projector. Finally, let <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}^{\perp}:=I_{d}-\Pi_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}^{\perp}:=I_{d}-\Pi_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the orthogonal projector onto the orthogonal complement of <math id="Thmtheorem5.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{span}(U_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>span</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{span}(U_{r})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, the following statements hold:</span></p>
<ol id="S2.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I4.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S2.I4.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(i)</span></span> 
<div id="S2.I4.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I4.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I4.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The PCA and exPCA subspaces coincide exactly (</span><math id="S2.I4.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}=\Pi_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}=\Pi_{r}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I4.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) if and only if the off-diagonal block of the perturbation vanishes:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I4.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S2.I4.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(ii)</span></span> 
<div id="S2.I4.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I4.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I4.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Whenever </span><math id="S2.I4.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I4.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the exPCA subspace is a non-trivial deformation of the standard PCA subspace, meaning </span><math id="S2.I4.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}\neq\Pi_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}\neq\Pi_{r}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I4.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S2.I4.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}(U_{r},U_{r}^{(\tau)})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}(U_{r},U_{r}^{(\tau)})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I4.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I4.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S2.I4.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(iii)</span></span> 
<div id="S2.I4.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I4.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I4.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For sufficiently small perturbations satisfying </span><math id="S2.I4.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta_{\tau}\|\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta_{\tau}\|\to 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I4.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the perturbed orthogonal projector admits the explicit first-order Taylor-Maclaurin Fréchet expansion:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{l}\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}-\Pi_{r}=\\
\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}\frac{u_{j}u_{j}^{\top}\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}+u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}\Delta_{\tau}u_{j}u_{j}^{\top}}{\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j}}+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{2}).\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{l}\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}-\Pi_{r}=\\
\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}\frac{u_{j}u_{j}^{\top}\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}+u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}\Delta_{\tau}u_{j}u_{j}^{\top}}{\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j}}+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{2}).\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I4.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S2.I4.ix4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(iv)</span></span> 
<div id="S2.I4.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I4.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I4.ix4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The resulting squared Grassmannian distance satisfies the asymptotic expansion:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}^{2}\left(U_{r},U_{r}^{(\tau)}\right)=\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}\frac{|\langle u_{j},\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}\rangle|^{2}}{(\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j})^{2}}+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{3})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}^{2}\left(U_{r},U_{r}^{(\tau)}\right)=\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}\frac{|\langle u_{j},\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}\rangle|^{2}}{(\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j})^{2}}+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{3}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I4.ix4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I4.ix4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which implies the absolute deterministic upper bound:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}\left(U_{r},U_{r}^{(\tau)}\right)\leq\frac{\|\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}\|_{F}}{\delta_{r}}+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}\left(U_{r},U_{r}^{(\tau)}\right)\leq\frac{\|\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}\|_{F}}{\delta_{r}}+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The bilinear block operator <math id="Thmtheorem5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> constitutes the unique, necessary, and sufficient first-order structural mechanism through which tail-risk information transfers from the variance-discarded complement directions into the retained dominant principal subspace.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Parts (i) and (ii):<span id="S2.SS6.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> By construction, the spectral decomposition yields <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\lambda_{i}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\lambda_{i}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>. The orthogonal projector <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}=\sum_{i=1}^{r}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}=\sum_{i=1}^{r}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> commutes with <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> because:</span></span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{l}\Sigma\Pi_{r}=\left(\sum_{i=1}^{d}\lambda_{i}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}\right)\left(\sum_{j=1}^{r}u_{j}u_{j}^{\top}\right)\\
=\sum_{i=1}^{r}\lambda_{i}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}=\left(\sum_{j=1}^{r}u_{j}u_{j}^{\top}\right)\left(\sum_{i=1}^{d}\lambda_{i}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}\right)\\
=\Pi_{r}\Sigma.\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{l}\Sigma\Pi_{r}=\left(\sum_{i=1}^{d}\lambda_{i}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}\right)\left(\sum_{j=1}^{r}u_{j}u_{j}^{\top}\right)\\
=\sum_{i=1}^{r}\lambda_{i}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}=\left(\sum_{j=1}^{r}u_{j}u_{j}^{\top}\right)\left(\sum_{i=1}^{d}\lambda_{i}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}\right)\\
=\Pi_{r}\Sigma.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> commute, and <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Pi_{r}=(I_{d}-\Pi_{r})\Pi_{r}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Pi_{r}=(I_{d}-\Pi_{r})\Pi_{r}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Sigma\Pi_{r}=\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Pi_{r}\Sigma=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Sigma\Pi_{r}=\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Pi_{r}\Sigma=0</annotation></semantics></math>, verifying that the standard PCA subspace <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}(\Pi_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}(\Pi_{r})</annotation></semantics></math> is an invariant subspace of <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now consider the perturbed operator <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\tau}=\Sigma+\Delta_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\tau}=\Sigma+\Delta_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>. A subspace characterized by an orthogonal projector <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is invariant under a linear operator <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I-P)AP=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I-P)AP=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}(\Pi_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}(\Pi_{r})</annotation></semantics></math> remains invariant under <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Sigma_{\tau}\Pi_{r}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Sigma_{\tau}\Pi_{r}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Expanding this product using the linears yields:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{l}\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Sigma_{\tau}\Pi_{r}=\Pi_{r}^{\perp}(\Sigma+\Delta_{\tau})\Pi_{r}\\
=\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Sigma\Pi_{r}+\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}=0+\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}\\
=\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}.\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{l}\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Sigma_{\tau}\Pi_{r}=\Pi_{r}^{\perp}(\Sigma+\Delta_{\tau})\Pi_{r}\\
=\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Sigma\Pi_{r}+\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}=0+\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}\\
=\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}=0</annotation></semantics></math> is the exact necessary and sufficient condition for <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}(\Pi_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}(\Pi_{r})</annotation></semantics></math> to be an invariant subspace of <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under the condition <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta_{\tau}\|&lt;\frac{\delta_{r}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta_{\tau}\|&lt;\frac{\delta_{r}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the spectrum of <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> is split into two disjoint sets separated by a gap. The dominant <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional eigenspace <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{r}^{(\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{r}^{(\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math> is unique. If <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, uniqueness dictates <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}=\Pi_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}=\Pi_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Conversely, if <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}(\Pi_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}(\Pi_{r})</annotation></semantics></math> is not invariant under <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>, so it cannot equal the true invariant eigenspace <math id="S2.SS6.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}(\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}(\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)})</annotation></semantics></math>, which proves Parts (i) and (ii).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Part (iii):<span id="S2.SS6.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Let <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma\subset\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\subset\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math> be a closed, positively oriented Jordan contour in the complex plane that encloses the dominant eigenvalues <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\lambda_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{r}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\lambda_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{r}\}</annotation></semantics></math> but excludes the remaining eigenvalues <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\lambda_{r+1},\ldots,\lambda_{d}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\lambda_{r+1},\ldots,\lambda_{d}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The distance from <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> to the spectrum of <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is lower bounded by <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\delta_{r}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\delta_{r}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, the resolvent <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(zI_{d}-\Sigma)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(zI_{d}-\Sigma)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> exists. By Riesz-Dunford holomorphic functional calculus, the unperturbed spectral projector is given by:</span></span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pi_{r}=-\frac{1}{2\pi i}\oint_{\Gamma}(zI_{d}-\Sigma)^{-1}dz." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mo rspace="0em">∮</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}=-\frac{1}{2\pi i}\oint_{\Gamma}(zI_{d}-\Sigma)^{-1}dz.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta_{\tau}\|&lt;\frac{\delta_{r}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta_{\tau}\|&lt;\frac{\delta_{r}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the perturbed resolvent can be written via the resolvent identity:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{l}(zI_{d}-\Sigma_{\tau})^{-1}=(zI_{d}-\Sigma-\Delta_{\tau})^{-1}\\
=(zI_{d}-\Sigma)^{-1}+(zI_{d}-\Sigma)^{-1}\Delta_{\tau}(zI_{d}-\Sigma)^{-1}+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{2}),\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{l}(zI_{d}-\Sigma_{\tau})^{-1}=(zI_{d}-\Sigma-\Delta_{\tau})^{-1}\\
=(zI_{d}-\Sigma)^{-1}+(zI_{d}-\Sigma)^{-1}\Delta_{\tau}(zI_{d}-\Sigma)^{-1}+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{2}),\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the remainder term <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> holds uniformly for <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. Integrating this series along <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> yields:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}=-\frac{1}{2\pi i}\oint_{\Gamma}(zI_{d}-\Sigma_{\tau})^{-1}dz=\Pi_{r}+\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mo rspace="0em">∮</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}=-\frac{1}{2\pi i}\oint_{\Gamma}(zI_{d}-\Sigma_{\tau})^{-1}dz=\Pi_{r}+\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the first-order Fréchet derivative map <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})=-\frac{1}{2\pi i}\oint_{\Gamma}(zI_{d}-\Sigma)^{-1}\Delta_{\tau}(zI_{d}-\Sigma)^{-1}dz." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mo rspace="0em">∮</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})=-\frac{1}{2\pi i}\oint_{\Gamma}(zI_{d}-\Sigma)^{-1}\Delta_{\tau}(zI_{d}-\Sigma)^{-1}dz.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting the spectral representation of the unperturbed resolvent <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(zI_{d}-\Sigma)^{-1}=\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{1}{z-\lambda_{k}}u_{k}u_{k}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(zI_{d}-\Sigma)^{-1}=\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{1}{z-\lambda_{k}}u_{k}u_{k}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> into the integral gives:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{l}\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})=\\
\sum_{k=1}^{d}\sum_{m=1}^{d}\left(-\frac{1}{2\pi i}\oint_{\Gamma}\frac{1}{(z-\lambda_{k})(z-\lambda_{m})}dz\right)u_{k}u_{k}^{\top}\Delta_{\tau}u_{m}u_{m}^{\top}.\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mo>∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mo>∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mo>∮</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{l}\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})=\\
\sum_{k=1}^{d}\sum_{m=1}^{d}\left(-\frac{1}{2\pi i}\oint_{\Gamma}\frac{1}{(z-\lambda_{k})(z-\lambda_{m})}dz\right)u_{k}u_{k}^{\top}\Delta_{\tau}u_{m}u_{m}^{\top}.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">By the residue theorem, the contour integral evaluates to <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> if both <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k},\lambda_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k},\lambda_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> are inside <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,m\leq r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,m\leq r</annotation></semantics></math>) or both are outside <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,m&gt;r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,m&gt;r</annotation></semantics></math>). When <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&gt;r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&gt;r</annotation></semantics></math>, the integrand has a single pole inside <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding a residue of <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}-\lambda_{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}-\lambda_{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Symmetrically, when <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leq r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leq r</annotation></semantics></math>, the pole is at <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\lambda_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\lambda_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, giving a residue of <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\lambda_{m}-\lambda_{k}}=-\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}-\lambda_{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\lambda_{m}-\lambda_{k}}=-\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}-\lambda_{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Evaluating these residues explicitly establishes Part (iii):</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})=\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}\frac{u_{j}u_{j}^{\top}\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}+u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}\Delta_{\tau}u_{j}u_{j}^{\top}}{\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})=\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}\frac{u_{j}u_{j}^{\top}\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}+u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}\Delta_{\tau}u_{j}u_{j}^{\top}}{\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Part (iv):<span id="S2.SS6.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> To calculate the Frobenius norm <math id="S2.SS6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}-\Pi_{r}\|_{F}^{2}=\operatorname{Tr}\left((\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}-\Pi_{r})^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}-\Pi_{r}\|_{F}^{2}=\operatorname{Tr}\left((\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}-\Pi_{r})^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> to first order, we examine the component <math id="S2.SS6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that <math id="S2.SS6.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{u_{k}u_{m}^{\top}\}_{k,m=1}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u_{k}u_{m}^{\top}\}_{k,m=1}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> forms an orthonormal basis for <math id="S2.SS6.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> under the Frobenius inner product <math id="S2.SS6.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle A,B\rangle_{F}=\operatorname{Tr}(A^{\top}B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle A,B\rangle_{F}=\operatorname{Tr}(A^{\top}B)</annotation></semantics></math>. The operator <math id="S2.SS6.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})</annotation></semantics></math> can be decomposed into two mutually orthogonal blocks:</span></span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{l}\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})=\mathbf{A}+\mathbf{A}^{\top},\quad\text{where}\\
\mathbf{A}=\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}\frac{u_{j}u_{j}^{\top}\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}}{\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j}}\\
=\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}\frac{u_{j}u_{j}^{\top}\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}}{\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j}}\right)\Pi_{r}.\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{l}\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})=\mathbf{A}+\mathbf{A}^{\top},\quad\text{where}\\
\mathbf{A}=\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}\frac{u_{j}u_{j}^{\top}\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}}{\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j}}\\
=\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}\frac{u_{j}u_{j}^{\top}\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}}{\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j}}\right)\Pi_{r}.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="S2.SS6.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}=\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\mathbf{A}\Pi_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}=\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\mathbf{A}\Pi_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS6.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}^{\top}=\Pi_{r}\mathbf{A}^{\top}\Pi_{r}^{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}^{\top}=\Pi_{r}\mathbf{A}^{\top}\Pi_{r}^{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>, their Frobenius inner product vanishes identically: <math id="S2.SS6.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{A}\mathbf{A})=\operatorname{Tr}(\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\mathbf{A}\Pi_{r}\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\mathbf{A}\Pi_{r})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{A}\mathbf{A})=\operatorname{Tr}(\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\mathbf{A}\Pi_{r}\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\mathbf{A}\Pi_{r})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. We obtain:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{l}\|\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})\|_{F}^{2}=\operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{A}\mathbf{A}^{\top})+\operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{A}^{\top}\mathbf{A})\\
=2\|\mathbf{A}\|_{F}^{2}\\
=2\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}\frac{|\langle u_{j},\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}\rangle|^{2}}{(\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j})^{2}}.\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐀𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐀</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{l}\|\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})\|_{F}^{2}=\operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{A}\mathbf{A}^{\top})+\operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{A}^{\top}\mathbf{A})\\
=2\|\mathbf{A}\|_{F}^{2}\\
=2\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}\frac{|\langle u_{j},\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}\rangle|^{2}}{(\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j})^{2}}.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Squaring the full perturbation expansion <math id="S2.SS6.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}-\Pi_{r}=\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}-\Pi_{r}=\mathcal{L}_{\Sigma}(\Delta_{\tau})+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and taking the trace yields:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}-\Pi_{r}\|_{F}^{2}=2\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}\frac{|\langle u_{j},\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}\rangle|^{2}}{(\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j})^{2}}+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}-\Pi_{r}\|_{F}^{2}=2\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}\frac{|\langle u_{j},\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}\rangle|^{2}}{(\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j})^{2}}+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">By Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition7" title="Definition 7 (Principal Angles and Grassmann Distance). ‣ II-F Geometric Subspace Misalignment Analysis ‣ II Problem Formulation ‣ The Risk Shadow of Principal Component Analysis: When 99.9999% Variance Preservation Causes Catastrophic Decision Errors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, the squared Grassmannian distance satisfies <math id="S2.SS6.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}^{2}(U_{r},U_{r}^{(\tau)})=\frac{1}{2}\|\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}-\Pi_{r}\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}^{2}(U_{r},U_{r}^{(\tau)})=\frac{1}{2}\|\Pi_{r}^{(\tau)}-\Pi_{r}\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Dividing the above expression by 2 gives the first equation in Part (iv).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, since <math id="S2.SS6.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}\geq\cdots\geq\lambda_{r}&gt;\lambda_{r+1}\geq\cdots\geq\lambda_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}\geq\cdots\geq\lambda_{r}&gt;\lambda_{r+1}\geq\cdots\geq\lambda_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that for all <math id="S2.SS6.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leq r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leq r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS6.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq r+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq r+1</annotation></semantics></math>, the denominator satisfies <math id="S2.SS6.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j})\geq(\lambda_{r}-\lambda_{r+1})=\delta_{r}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j})\geq(\lambda_{r}-\lambda_{r+1})=\delta_{r}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Factoring out this minimum spectral gap yields:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}^{2}\left(U_{r},U_{r}^{(\tau)}\right)\leq\frac{1}{\delta_{r}^{2}}\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}|\langle u_{j},\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}\rangle|^{2}+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}^{2}\left(U_{r},U_{r}^{(\tau)}\right)\leq\frac{1}{\delta_{r}^{2}}\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}|\langle u_{j},\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}\rangle|^{2}+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Observe that the double summation is exactly the squared Frobenius norm of the off-diagonal block projection of <math id="S2.SS6.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{l}\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}|\langle u_{j},\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}\rangle|^{2}\\
=\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}\|u_{j}u_{j}^{\top}\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}\|_{F}^{2}\\
=\left\|\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}\right\|_{F}^{2}.\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{l}\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}|\langle u_{j},\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}\rangle|^{2}\\
=\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sum_{j=r+1}^{d}\|u_{j}u_{j}^{\top}\Delta_{\tau}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}\|_{F}^{2}\\
=\left\|\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}\right\|_{F}^{2}.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this back into the inequality produces:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}^{2}\left(U_{r},U_{r}^{(\tau)}\right)\leq\frac{\|\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}\|_{F}^{2}}{\delta_{r}^{2}}+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}^{2}\left(U_{r},U_{r}^{(\tau)}\right)\leq\frac{\|\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}\|_{F}^{2}}{\delta_{r}^{2}}+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the square root of both sides via the Taylor expansion <math id="S2.SS6.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{x^{2}+\epsilon}=x+O(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{x^{2}+\epsilon}=x+O(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> establishes the final bounded inequality:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}\left(U_{r},U_{r}^{(\tau)}\right)\leq\frac{\|\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}\|_{F}}{\delta_{r}}+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}\left(U_{r},U_{r}^{(\tau)}\right)\leq\frac{\|\Pi_{r}^{\perp}\Delta_{\tau}\Pi_{r}\|_{F}}{\delta_{r}}+O(\|\Delta_{\tau}\|^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">which concludes the proof of the theorem.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">III </span><span id="S3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Decision-Theoretic Subspace Learning: exp2PCA</span></h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To resolve the fundamental alignment mismatch between geometric reconstruction and task-specific penalties, we introduce <span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">exp2PCA</span> (<span id="S3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Expectile of Misclassification Cost PCA</span>). This framework directly optimizes the <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-expectile of the downstream misclassification cost over the joint data-label space. By targeting the tail risk of the actual decision penalty rather than an indirect geometric summary statistic, exp2PCA systematically maintains robust decision boundaries, even when rare, high-stakes events manifest exclusively along directions of minor global variance.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now formalize the complete multiclass setting (<math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>) to establish the structural conditions under which classical global variance maximization fails catastrophically compared to direct decision-theoretic risk minimization. Let <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{K-1}=\{p\in\mathbb{R}^{K}_{\geq 0}:\sum_{k=1}^{K}p_{k}=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{K-1}=\{p\in\mathbb{R}^{K}_{\geq 0}:\sum_{k=1}^{K}p_{k}=1\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the topological <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(K-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional probability simplex. For any conditional probability vector <math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\Delta^{K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\Delta^{K-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal Bayes decision operator minimizing the conditional expected cost is defined as:</p>
<table id="S3.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(p)=\arg\min_{a\in\{1,\dots,K\}}\sum_{b=1}^{K}C_{ab}\,p_{b}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(p)=\arg\min_{a\in\{1,\dots,K\}}\sum_{b=1}^{K}C_{ab}\,p_{b}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 8</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Conditional Support of a Random Vector)<span id="Thmdefinition8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a random vector and <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y:\Omega\to\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y:\Omega\to\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math> be a categorical random variable on a complete probability space <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\mathbb{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\mathbb{P})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is endowed with the standard Euclidean topology. Let <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the regular conditional probability distribution of <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> given the event <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{Y=k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{Y=k\}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as the unique probability measure on the Borel <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying:</p>
<table id="S3.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{l}\mu_{k}(B)=\mathbb{P}(X\in B\mid Y=k)=\frac{\mathbb{P}(X\in B,Y=k)}{\mathbb{P}(Y=k)}\\
\forall B\in\mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}^{d}).\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{l}\mu_{k}(B)=\mathbb{P}(X\in B\mid Y=k)=\frac{\mathbb{P}(X\in B,Y=k)}{\mathbb{P}(Y=k)}\\
\forall B\in\mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}^{d}).\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The conditional support of <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=k</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted as <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{supp}(X\mid Y=k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{supp}(X\mid Y=k)</annotation></semantics></math>, is defined as the topological support of the conditional measure <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Formally, it is the intersection of all closed sets in <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> of full <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-measure:</p>
<table id="S3.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{supp}(X\mid Y=k)=\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\mu_{k}\left(B_{\epsilon}(x)\right)&gt;0\quad\forall\epsilon&gt;0\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{supp}(X\mid Y=k)=\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\mu_{k}\left(B_{\epsilon}(x)\right)&gt;0\quad\forall\epsilon&gt;0\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition8.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\epsilon}(x)=\{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\|y-x\|_{2}&lt;\epsilon\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\epsilon}(x)=\{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\|y-x\|_{2}&lt;\epsilon\}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the open Euclidean ball of radius <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> centered at <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 3</span></span><span id="Thmremark3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By construction, <math id="Thmremark3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{supp}(X\mid Y=k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{supp}(X\mid Y=k)</annotation></semantics></math> is a closed subset of <math id="Thmremark3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. It explicitly defines the smallest closed region of the space where the random vector <math id="Thmremark3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> manifests with strictly positive probability density or mass when conditioned on belonging to class <math id="Thmremark3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 9</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Linear Subspace Mapping of Topological Support)<span id="Thmdefinition9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{*}\in\mathcal{U}_{r}=\{P\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times r}:P^{\top}P=I_{r}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{*}\in\mathcal{U}_{r}=\{P\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times r}:P^{\top}P=I_{r}\}</annotation></semantics></math> represent a semi-orthogonal matrix defining a continuous linear projection map <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> given by <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x)=P_{*}^{\top}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x)=P_{*}^{\top}x</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{m}=\text{supp}(X\mid Y=m)\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{m}=\text{supp}(X\mid Y=m)\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the closed conditional topological support of the random vector <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> given class <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>. The expression <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{*}^{\top}\left(\mathcal{S}_{m}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{*}^{\top}\left(\mathcal{S}_{m}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the forward image of the set <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as:</p>
<table id="S3.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{l}P_{*}^{\top}\left(\text{supp}(X\mid Y=m)\right)=\\
\left\{z\in\mathbb{R}^{r}:\exists x\in\text{supp}(X\mid Y=m)\text{ such that }z=P_{*}^{\top}x\right\}.\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> such that </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{l}P_{*}^{\top}\left(\text{supp}(X\mid Y=m)\right)=\\
\left\{z\in\mathbb{R}^{r}:\exists x\in\text{supp}(X\mid Y=m)\text{ such that }z=P_{*}^{\top}x\right\}.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2</span></span><span id="Thmproposition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Topological and Structural Properties of the Projected Support)<span id="Thmproposition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x)=P_{*}^{\top}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x)=P_{*}^{\top}x</annotation></semantics></math> be the projection mapping, and let <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{m}=\text{supp}(X\mid Y=m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{m}=\text{supp}(X\mid Y=m)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the following properties hold:</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Preservation of Connectedness:</span><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> If </span><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a connected (or path-connected) subset of </span><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then its projected image </span><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{*}^{\top}(\mathcal{S}_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{*}^{\top}(\mathcal{S}_{m})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a connected (or path-connected) subset of </span><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Boundedness and Compactness:</span><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> If </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a bounded subset of </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, it is compact (by the Heine-Borel theorem). Because </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a continuous linear operator, the projected image </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{*}^{\top}(\mathcal{S}_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{*}^{\top}(\mathcal{S}_{m})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is compact, and therefore closed and bounded in </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Convexity Translucency:</span><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> If </span><math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a convex set in </span><math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, its low-dimensional footprint </span><math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{*}^{\top}(\mathcal{S}_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{*}^{\top}(\mathcal{S}_{m})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> preserves convexity in </span><math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Property (1) follows because the forward image of a connected space under any continuous function is connected. Property (2) arises because the continuous image of a compact set is compact; since <math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is a Hausdorff space, compactness guarantees that the set <math id="S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{*}^{\top}(\mathcal{S}_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{*}^{\top}(\mathcal{S}_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> is closed, which ensures that the boundary elements are well-defined in the compressed space. Property (3) follows directly from the linearity of the projection operator: for any <math id="S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},z_{2}\in P_{*}^{\top}(\mathcal{S}_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},z_{2}\in P_{*}^{\top}(\mathcal{S}_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, there exist <math id="S3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},x_{2}\in\mathcal{S}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},x_{2}\in\mathcal{S}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}=P_{*}^{\top}x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}=P_{*}^{\top}x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{2}=P_{*}^{\top}x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{2}=P_{*}^{\top}x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="S3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, the linear combination satisfies <math id="S3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha z_{1}+(1-\alpha)z_{2}=P_{*}^{\top}(\alpha x_{1}+(1-\alpha)x_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha z_{1}+(1-\alpha)z_{2}=P_{*}^{\top}(\alpha x_{1}+(1-\alpha)x_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, which resides in the forward image due to the convexity of <math id="S3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The following theorem provides a distribution-free, non-asymmetric guarantee establishing the strict dominance of exp2PCA over standard principal component representations.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Strict Dominance of exp2PCA )<span id="Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a square-integrable random vector, and let <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\in\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\in\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math> be a categorical label with prior probabilities <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}=\mathbb{P}(Y=k)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}=\mathbb{P}(Y=k)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}^{K\times K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}^{K\times K}</annotation></semantics></math> be a fixed cost matrix satisfying <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{aa}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{aa}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{ab}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{ab}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\neq b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\neq b</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume there exists a critical target risk class <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math> characterized by an extreme misclassification penalty relative to all other alternatives:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{a\neq m}C_{am}\gg\max_{a\neq m,b\neq m}C_{ab}\ \text{and}\quad\min_{a\neq m}C_{am}&gt;\max_{b\neq m}C_{mb}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≫</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{a\neq m}C_{am}\gg\max_{a\neq m,b\neq m}C_{ab}\ \text{and}\quad\min_{a\neq m}C_{am}&gt;\max_{b\neq m}C_{mb}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose the joint distribution <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{(X,Y)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{(X,Y)}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the following structural axioms:</span></p>
<ul id="S3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Information Erasure:</span><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> The critical target class </span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is statistically independent of the leading </span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-dimensional PCA subspace, which is formally encoded as:
</span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Y\cdot\mathbf{1}_{\{Y=m\}}\perp\!\!\!\perp P_{\text{PCA}}^{\top}X." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⟂</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">PCA</mtext></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\cdot\mathbf{1}_{\{Y=m\}}\perp\!\!\!\perp P_{\text{PCA}}^{\top}X.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Subspace Discriminability:</span><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> There exists an alternative semi-orthogonal matrix </span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{*}\in\mathcal{U}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{*}\in\mathcal{U}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and a Borel-measurable partitioning boundary </span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma\subset\mathbb{R}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\subset\mathbb{R}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that the projection of the support of class </span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is perfectly separable from the union of all other classes:
</span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{*}^{\top}\left(\text{supp}(X\mid Y=m)\right)\cap P_{*}^{\top}\left(\bigcup_{k\neq m}\text{supp}(X\mid Y=k)\right)=\emptyset." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{*}^{\top}\left(\text{supp}(X\mid Y=m)\right)\cap P_{*}^{\top}\left(\bigcup_{k\neq m}\text{supp}(X\mid Y=k)\right)=\emptyset.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, there exists a lower-bound threshold <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{0}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{0}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all tail parameters <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in(\tau_{0},1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in(\tau_{0},1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimized exp2PCA risk strictly dominates the PCA risk:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{\text{exp2}},h)&lt;\min_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{\text{PCA}},h)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">exp2</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">PCA</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{\text{exp2}},h)&lt;\min_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{\text{PCA}},h).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The geometric and decision-theoretic optimal subspaces diverge: <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{exp2}}\neq P_{\text{PCA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">exp2</mtext></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">PCA</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{exp2}}\neq P_{\text{PCA}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\text{PCA}}=P_{\text{PCA}}^{\top}X\in\mathbb{R}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\text{PCA}}=P_{\text{PCA}}^{\top}X\in\mathbb{R}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the compressed representation space. By the Information Erasure axiom, the conditional distribution of the target class label given the PCA embedding collapses to its prior probability, yielding <math id="S3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(Y=m\mid Z_{\text{PCA}})=\pi_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(Y=m\mid Z_{\text{PCA}})=\pi_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider an arbitrary measurable classifier <math id="S3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> operating on <math id="S3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\text{PCA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\text{PCA}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We evaluate the conditional distribution of the random decision loss <math id="S3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(P_{\text{PCA}},h)=C_{h(Z_{\text{PCA}}),Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(P_{\text{PCA}},h)=C_{h(Z_{\text{PCA}}),Y}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any realization of <math id="S3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\text{PCA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\text{PCA}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the classifier must select an action <math id="S3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=h(Z_{\text{PCA}})\in\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=h(Z_{\text{PCA}})\in\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We analyze the two structural cases for this action selection:</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 1 (<math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=m</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> If the classifier selects the critical class action, the true state cannot be <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\pi_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\pi_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. The loss <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded from above by <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{b\neq m}C_{mb}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{b\neq m}C_{mb}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{mm}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{mm}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the loss takes values in the interval <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,\max_{b\neq m}C_{mb}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\max_{b\neq m}C_{mb}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 2 (<math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\neq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\neq m</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> If the classifier selects any non-critical action, the system runs the risk of misclassifying the critical state. With a strictly positive conditional probability <math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{m}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{m}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the true state is <math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=m</annotation></semantics></math>, which triggers an immediate catastrophic loss of <math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{am}\geq\min_{a\neq m}C_{am}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{am}\geq\min_{a\neq m}C_{am}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\min_{h}\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{\text{PCA}},h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\min_{h}\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{\text{PCA}},h)</annotation></semantics></math> be the optimized tail risk on the PCA subspace. Recall that the expectile functional is characterized by the integration condition <math id="S3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[w_{\tau}(L;t)(L-t)]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[w_{\tau}(L;t)(L-t)]=0</annotation></semantics></math>. As <math id="S3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\to 1^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\to 1^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>, the weight function prioritizes the essential supremum of the support.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(Z_{\text{PCA}})\neq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(Z_{\text{PCA}})\neq m</annotation></semantics></math>, the loss distribution contains a mass at or above <math id="S3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{a\neq m}C_{am}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{a\neq m}C_{am}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(Z_{\text{PCA}})=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(Z_{\text{PCA}})=m</annotation></semantics></math>, the maximum possible loss is <math id="S3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{b\neq m}C_{mb}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{b\neq m}C_{mb}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the cost asymmetry condition established in (<a href="#S3.E28" title="In Theorem 6 (Strict Dominance of exp2PCA ). ‣ III Decision-Theoretic Subspace Learning: exp2PCA ‣ The Risk Shadow of Principal Component Analysis: When 99.9999% Variance Preservation Causes Catastrophic Decision Errors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>), the essential supremum under any action <math id="S3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\neq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\neq m</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly larger than under <math id="S3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=m</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, to minimize the asymmetric quadratic penalty under extreme tail weights <math id="S3.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\to 1^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\to 1^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>, the first-order condition forces the optimal classifier to select <math id="S3.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\text{PCA}}(Z_{\text{PCA}})\equiv m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\text{PCA}}(Z_{\text{PCA}})\equiv m</annotation></semantics></math>. Evaluating the exact limit under this action yields:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}\lim_{\tau\to 1^{-}}\min_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{\text{PCA}},h)\\
=\mathbb{E}[C_{m,Y}\mid Y\neq m]=\sum_{b\neq m}C_{mb}\frac{\pi_{b}}{1-\pi_{m}}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}\lim_{\tau\to 1^{-}}\min_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{\text{PCA}},h)\\
=\mathbb{E}[C_{m,Y}\mid Y\neq m]=\sum_{b\neq m}C_{mb}\frac{\pi_{b}}{1-\pi_{m}}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the core properties of the expectile functional under bounded variables, for any <math id="S3.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently close to <math id="S3.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, the risk is lower-bounded by the expectation over the non-zero support:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{\text{PCA}},h)\geq\sum_{b\neq m}C_{mb}\pi_{b}&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{\text{PCA}},h)\geq\sum_{b\neq m}C_{mb}\pi_{b}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, examine the exp2PCA optimization space. By the Subspace Discriminability axiom, we can instantiate the alternative projection matrix <math id="S3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{exp2}}=P_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>exp2</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{exp2}}=P_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Because the critical class <math id="S3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is perfectly isolated in this subspace, we can construct a customized, measurable indicator classifier <math id="S3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{*}\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{*}\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> defined as:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{*}(P_{*}^{\top}X)=\begin{cases}m\ \text{if }P_{*}^{\top}X\in P_{*}^{\top}\left(\text{supp}(X\mid Y=m)\right),\\
\psi\left(\mathbb{P}(Y\mid P_{*}^{\top}X,Y\neq m)\right)\ \text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{*}(P_{*}^{\top}X)=\begin{cases}m\ \text{if }P_{*}^{\top}X\in P_{*}^{\top}\left(\text{supp}(X\mid Y=m)\right),\\
\psi\left(\mathbb{P}(Y\mid P_{*}^{\top}X,Y\neq m)\right)\ \text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">We evaluate the complete random loss distribution under this joint configuration <math id="S3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{*},h_{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{*},h_{*})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<ul id="S3.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=m</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{*}^{\top}X\in P_{*}^{\top}\left(\text{supp}(X\mid Y=m)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{*}^{\top}X\in P_{*}^{\top}\left(\text{supp}(X\mid Y=m)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies <math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{*}(P_{*}^{\top}X)=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{*}(P_{*}^{\top}X)=m</annotation></semantics></math>. The loss evaluates exactly to <math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(P_{*},h_{*})=C_{mm}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(P_{*},h_{*})=C_{mm}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\neq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\neq m</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{*}^{\top}X\notin P_{*}^{\top}\left(\text{supp}(X\mid Y=m)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{*}^{\top}X\notin P_{*}^{\top}\left(\text{supp}(X\mid Y=m)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, implying <math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{*}(P_{*}^{\top}X)\neq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{*}(P_{*}^{\top}X)\neq m</annotation></semantics></math>. This structural protection completely prevents the occurrence of a catastrophic False Negative event for the critical class. The decision loss is thus strictly bounded from above by the minor inter-class penalties:</p>
<table id="S3.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(P_{*},h_{*})\leq\max_{a\neq m,b\neq m}C_{ab}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(P_{*},h_{*})\leq\max_{a\neq m,b\neq m}C_{ab}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S3.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Because the random variable <math id="S3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(P_{*},h_{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(P_{*},h_{*})</annotation></semantics></math> is zero whenever <math id="S3.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=m</annotation></semantics></math> and bounded by <math id="S3.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{a\neq m,b\neq m}C_{ab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{a\neq m,b\neq m}C_{ab}</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise, its absolute essential supremum satisfies <math id="S3.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ess\,sup}\,L(P_{*},h_{*})\leq\max_{a\neq m,b\neq m}C_{ab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>ess sup</mtext><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ess\,sup}\,L(P_{*},h_{*})\leq\max_{a\neq m,b\neq m}C_{ab}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the monotonic property of the expectile operator with respect to stochastic dominance, we have:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{*},h_{*})\leq\max_{a\neq m,b\neq m}C_{ab}\quad\forall\tau\in(0,1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{*},h_{*})\leq\max_{a\neq m,b\neq m}C_{ab}\quad\forall\tau\in(0,1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">By the structural assumption stated in (<a href="#S3.E28" title="In Theorem 6 (Strict Dominance of exp2PCA ). ‣ III Decision-Theoretic Subspace Learning: exp2PCA ‣ The Risk Shadow of Principal Component Analysis: When 99.9999% Variance Preservation Causes Catastrophic Decision Errors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>), namely, that the collective conditional average of the minority class penalties is strictly greater than the maximum localized interaction among the majority classes, we combine the inequalities to show:</span></p>
<table id="S3.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{l}\min_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{\text{exp2}},h)\leq\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{*},h_{*})\\
\leq\max_{a\neq m,b\neq m}C_{ab}\\
&lt;\min_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{\text{PCA}},h),\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>exp2</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{l}\min_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{\text{exp2}},h)\leq\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{*},h_{*})\\
\leq\max_{a\neq m,b\neq m}C_{ab}\\
&lt;\min_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{\text{PCA}},h),\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p9.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p9.5.1" class="ltx_text">which holds robustly for all <math id="S3.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\geq\tau_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\geq\tau_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Because the infimum of the joint exp2PCA objective function achieves a strictly lower tail risk than any solution restricted to the standard PCA subspace, the optimal projection operators cannot coincide. Thus, <math id="S3.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{exp2}}\neq P_{\text{PCA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>exp2</mtext></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{exp2}}\neq P_{\text{PCA}}</annotation></semantics></math>, completing the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">VC dimension.</span>
Let <math id="S3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> be a class of functions <math id="S3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a set <math id="S3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\{x_{1},\dots,x_{m}\}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\{x_{1},\dots,x_{m}\}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, define
<math id="S3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}|_{S}=\{(h(x_{1}),\dots,h(x_{m})):h\in\mathcal{H}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}|_{S}=\{(h(x_{1}),\dots,h(x_{m})):h\in\mathcal{H}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="S3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="S3.p10.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">shattered</em> by <math id="S3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{H}|_{S}|=2^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{H}|_{S}|=2^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then</p>
<table id="S3.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{l}\mathrm{VC}(\mathcal{H})\\
=\sup\left\{m\in\mathbb{N}\;:\;\exists S\subset\mathbb{R}^{d},\ |S|=m,\ S\text{ shattered by }\mathcal{H}\right\},\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>VC</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>S</mi><mtext> shattered by </mtext><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{l}\mathrm{VC}(\mathcal{H})\\
=\sup\left\{m\in\mathbb{N}\;:\;\exists S\subset\mathbb{R}^{d},\ |S|=m,\ S\text{ shattered by }\mathcal{H}\right\},\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p10.2" class="ltx_p">with the convention <math id="S3.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{VC}(\mathcal{H})=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>VC</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{VC}(\mathcal{H})=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> if the supremum is unbounded.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">III-A</span> </span><span id="S3.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Generalization Bounds for Decision Space Risk</span></h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 7</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">To guarantee that the subspace alignment learned by exp2PCA transfers to unseen data drawn from the joint distribution <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{(X,Y)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{(X,Y)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we establish uniform concentration bounds for the joint risk over the Stiefel-classifier manifold <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{r}\times\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{r}\times\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{n}=\{(X_{i},Y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{n}=\{(X_{i},Y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be an i.i.d. training sample. For a subspace <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in\mathcal{U}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in\mathcal{U}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> (Stiefel manifold of <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional orthonormal bases in <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>) and a classifier <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the misclassification cost
<math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{P,h}(X,Y)=C_{h(P^{\top}X),\,Y}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{P,h}(X,Y)=C_{h(P^{\top}X),\,Y},</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is a cost matrix satisfying <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq C_{ab}\leq M_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq C_{ab}\leq M_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b</annotation></semantics></math>.
The <em id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">empirical tail-expectile risk</em> at level <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{R}}_{n,\tau}(P,h)=\arg\min_{t\in\mathbb{R}}\;\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\ell_{\tau}\!\bigl(L_{P,h}(X_{i},Y_{i})-t\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{R}}_{n,\tau}(P,h)=\arg\min_{t\in\mathbb{R}}\;\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\ell_{\tau}\!\bigl(L_{P,h}(X_{i},Y_{i})-t\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math>
The corresponding true risk <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P,h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P,h)</annotation></semantics></math> replaces the empirical average by the expectation <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔼</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume that the classifier class <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> has finite VC dimension <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{VC}(\mathcal{H})&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>VC</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{VC}(\mathcal{H})&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, for any <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the solution <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{\text{exp2}},h_{\text{exp2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">exp2</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">exp2</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{\text{exp2}},h_{\text{exp2}})</annotation></semantics></math> obtained by <span id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">exp2PCA</span> satisfies, with probability at least <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{l}\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{\text{exp2}},h_{\text{exp2}})\\
\;\leq\;\widehat{\mathcal{R}}_{n,\tau}(P_{\text{exp2}},h_{\text{exp2}})\\
\;+\;\frac{2M_{\max}}{\min(\tau,1-\tau)}\,\sqrt{\frac{r(d-r)+\mathrm{VC}(\mathcal{H})\log(n/d)}{n}}\\
\;+\;M_{\max}\sqrt{\frac{\log(1/\delta)}{2n}}.\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">exp2</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">exp2</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">exp2</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">exp2</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>VC</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{l}\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P_{\text{exp2}},h_{\text{exp2}})\\
\;\leq\;\widehat{\mathcal{R}}_{n,\tau}(P_{\text{exp2}},h_{\text{exp2}})\\
\;+\;\frac{2M_{\max}}{\min(\tau,1-\tau)}\,\sqrt{\frac{r(d-r)+\mathrm{VC}(\mathcal{H})\log(n/d)}{n}}\\
\;+\;M_{\max}\sqrt{\frac{\log(1/\delta)}{2n}}.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof proceeds in three steps.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">1. Lipschitz property of the expectile functional.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any random variable <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> bounded by <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, the map <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\mapsto e_{\tau}(L)=\arg\min_{t}\mathbb{E}[\ell_{\tau}(L-t)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\mapsto e_{\tau}(L)=\arg\min_{t}\mathbb{E}[\ell_{\tau}(L-t)]</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\min(\tau,1-\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\min(\tau,1-\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz with respect to the <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-distance.
Indeed, the function <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\mapsto\mathbb{E}[\ell_{\tau}(L-t)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\mapsto\mathbb{E}[\ell_{\tau}(L-t)]</annotation></semantics></math> is strongly convex with modulus <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\min(\tau,1-\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\min(\tau,1-\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>, so</p>
<table id="S3.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|e_{\tau}(L)-e_{\tau}(L^{\prime})|\leq\frac{1}{\min(\tau,1-\tau)}\,\mathbb{E}[|L-L^{\prime}|]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|e_{\tau}(L)-e_{\tau}(L^{\prime})|\leq\frac{1}{\min(\tau,1-\tau)}\,\mathbb{E}[|L-L^{\prime}|].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Applying this to the true and empirical distributions of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{P,h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{P,h}</annotation></semantics></math> yields</p>
<table id="S3.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P,h)-\widehat{\mathcal{R}}_{n,\tau}(P,h)|\leq\frac{1}{\min(\tau,1-\tau)}\,\mathbb{E}_{n}\bigl[|L_{P,h}-\mathbb{E}[L_{P,h}]|\bigr]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{R}_{\tau}(P,h)-\widehat{\mathcal{R}}_{n,\tau}(P,h)|\leq\frac{1}{\min(\tau,1-\tau)}\,\mathbb{E}_{n}\bigl[|L_{P,h}-\mathbb{E}[L_{P,h}]|\bigr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the empirical expectation.
Because <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq L_{P,h}\leq M_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq L_{P,h}\leq M_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can bound the right-hand side by</p>
<table id="S3.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{2M_{\max}}{\min(\tau,1-\tau)}\,\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\bigl|\mathbb{E}_{n}[f]-\mathbb{E}[f]\bigr|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2M_{\max}}{\min(\tau,1-\tau)}\,\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\bigl|\mathbb{E}_{n}[f]-\mathbb{E}[f]\bigr|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{F}=\{(X,Y)\mapsto L_{P,h}(X,Y):P\in\mathcal{U}_{r},\;h\in\mathcal{H}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}=\{(X,Y)\mapsto L_{P,h}(X,Y):P\in\mathcal{U}_{r},\;h\in\mathcal{H}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">2. Uniform concentration over <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The function class <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is a composition of the linear projection <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\top}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\top}X</annotation></semantics></math> (parameterised by <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>), the classifier <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, and the bounded cost matrix.
The Stiefel manifold <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> has dimension <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(d-r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(d-r)</annotation></semantics></math>, leading to covering numbers <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\mathcal{U}_{r},\epsilon)\leq(c_{1}/\epsilon)^{r(d-r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\mathcal{U}_{r},\epsilon)\leq(c_{1}/\epsilon)^{r(d-r)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The VC class <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> yields covering numbers <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\mathcal{H},\epsilon,\mathcal{D}_{n})\leq(c_{2}n/\epsilon)^{\mathrm{VC}(\mathcal{H})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>VC</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\mathcal{H},\epsilon,\mathcal{D}_{n})\leq(c_{2}n/\epsilon)^{\mathrm{VC}(\mathcal{H})}</annotation></semantics></math> for the empirical <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> metric.
By composing these, the covering number of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</p>
<table id="S3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\mathcal{N}(\mathcal{F},\epsilon,\mathcal{D}_{n})\lesssim\bigl(r(d-r)+\mathrm{VC}(\mathcal{H})\log(n/\epsilon)\bigr)\log(1/\epsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>VC</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\mathcal{N}(\mathcal{F},\epsilon,\mathcal{D}_{n})\lesssim\bigl(r(d-r)+\mathrm{VC}(\mathcal{H})\log(n/\epsilon)\bigr)\log(1/\epsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Dudley’s entropy integral then bounds the Rademacher complexity:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}_{n}(\mathcal{F})\leq C\sqrt{\frac{r(d-r)+\mathrm{VC}(\mathcal{H})\log(n/d)}{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℜ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>VC</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}_{n}(\mathcal{F})\leq C\sqrt{\frac{r(d-r)+\mathrm{VC}(\mathcal{H})\log(n/d)}{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Standard concentration gives, with probability at least <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\bigl|\mathbb{E}_{n}[f]-\mathbb{E}[f]\bigr|\leq 2\mathfrak{R}_{n}(\mathcal{F})+M_{\max}\sqrt{\frac{\log(1/\delta)}{2n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℜ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\bigl|\mathbb{E}_{n}[f]-\mathbb{E}[f]\bigr|\leq 2\mathfrak{R}_{n}(\mathcal{F})+M_{\max}\sqrt{\frac{\log(1/\delta)}{2n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">3. Putting everything together.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Combining the Lipschitz bound with the uniform concentration estimate and plugging in the specific <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{\text{exp2}},h_{\text{exp2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>exp2</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>exp2</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{\text{exp2}},h_{\text{exp2}})</annotation></semantics></math> yields the stated inequality.
The term <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{2M_{\max}}{\min(\tau,1-\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2M_{\max}}{\min(\tau,1-\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math> accounts for the sensitivity of the expectile under asymmetric tail weighting, while the remaining terms capture the estimation error due to finite samples and the complexity of the joint representation, classifier space.
Thus, <span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">exp2PCA</span> generalises robustly even for extreme asymmetry (<math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\to 1^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\to 1^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>).
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Explicit Synthetic Benchmarks (2D, <math id="S4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=1</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We analyze a pathological continuous geometric distribution in <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to evaluate a rank-1 projection vector <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=(\cos\theta,\sin\theta)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=(\cos\theta,\sin\theta)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. This scenario provides fully analytical proofs demonstrating how unsupervised frameworks and even class-weighted extensions like TP-PCA, can lose critical discriminative signals, whereas the decision-theoretic exp2PCA framework seamlessly recovers them.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span> </span><span id="S4.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Continuous Asymmetric Gaussian Mixture Distribution</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let the generative distribution of the random vector <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=(x_{1},x_{2})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=(x_{1},x_{2})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> be a mixture of a highly dispersed majority class (<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=0</annotation></semantics></math>) and a tightly clustered, structurally shifted rare class (<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=1</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<ul id="S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Class 0</span> (<math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}=0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}=0.99</annotation></semantics></math>): <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X\mid Y=0\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\begin{pmatrix}0\\
0\end{pmatrix},\Sigma_{0}\right),\quad\Sigma_{0}=\begin{pmatrix}100&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>100</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\mid Y=0\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\begin{pmatrix}0\\
0\end{pmatrix},\Sigma_{0}\right),\quad\Sigma_{0}=\begin{pmatrix}100&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Class 1</span> (<math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>): <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X\mid Y=1\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\begin{pmatrix}0\\
\mu_{1}\end{pmatrix},\Sigma_{1}\right),\quad\mu_{1}=5,\;\Sigma_{1}=\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\
0&amp;0.1\end{pmatrix}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0.1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\mid Y=1\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\begin{pmatrix}0\\
\mu_{1}\end{pmatrix},\Sigma_{1}\right),\quad\mu_{1}=5,\;\Sigma_{1}=\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\
0&amp;0.1\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The cost profile is parameterized by asymmetric penalties <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FN}=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FN}=100</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FP}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FP}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, with the risk metric evaluated at the extreme upper tail parameter <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.99</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">IV-B</span> </span><span id="S4.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Analytical Evaluation across Dimensionality Reduction Paradigms</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">1. Standard PCA
Standard unsupervised PCA constructs its rank-1 subspace by isolating the leading eigenvector of the global covariance matrix <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{total}}=\begin{pmatrix}99.01&amp;0\\
0&amp;1.2385\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>99.01</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1.2385</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{total}}=\begin{pmatrix}99.01&amp;0\\
0&amp;1.2385\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{total}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{total}}</annotation></semantics></math> is perfectly diagonal with <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}=99.01\gg\lambda_{2}=1.2385" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>99.01</mn><mo>≫</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.2385</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}=99.01\gg\lambda_{2}=1.2385</annotation></semantics></math>, the unique optimal projection vector is:</p>
<table id="S4.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\text{PCA}}=\begin{pmatrix}1\\
0\end{pmatrix},\quad\text{corresponding to }\theta^{*}=0^{\circ}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>corresponding to </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\text{PCA}}=\begin{pmatrix}1\\
0\end{pmatrix},\quad\text{corresponding to }\theta^{*}=0^{\circ}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The compressed variable collapses to the horizontal coordinate <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=u_{\text{PCA}}^{\top}X=x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=u_{\text{PCA}}^{\top}X=x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under this projection, both classes map directly on top of each other centered at <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, making the rare class completely unresolvable. The optimal decision rule collapses to the constant majority assignment <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(z)\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(z)\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>, incurring a False Negative penalty of <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FN}=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FN}=100</annotation></semantics></math> with a probability exactly equal to the rare class prevalence <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Solving the implicit first-order stationarity condition for the <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.99</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.99</annotation></semantics></math>-expectile <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=e_{0.99}(L_{\text{PCA}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0.99</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=e_{0.99}(L_{\text{PCA}})</annotation></semantics></math> yields:
<math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{0.99}(L_{\text{PCA}})=50.0000." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0.99</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>50.0000</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{0.99}(L_{\text{PCA}})=50.0000.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Tail-Preserving PCA (TP-PCA)</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">TP-PCA modifies standard PCA by introducing an explicit, supervised class-weighting scheme designed to amplify the second-moment footprint of the rare target class <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}_{R}=\{1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}_{R}=\{1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The sample weights are defined as <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w_{i}=1+\alpha\mathbf{1}_{\{Y_{i}=1\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}=1+\alpha\mathbf{1}_{\{Y_{i}=1\}}</annotation></semantics></math> for an inflation hyperparameter <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By the strong law of large numbers, the empirical weighted mean vector converges almost surely to its asymptotic expectation:</p>
<table id="S4.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{w}=\frac{\mathbb{E}[w(Y)X]}{\mathbb{E}[w(Y)]}=\begin{pmatrix}0\\
\frac{5\pi_{1}(1+\alpha)}{1+\alpha\pi_{1}}\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{w}=\frac{\mathbb{E}[w(Y)X]}{\mathbb{E}[w(Y)]}=\begin{pmatrix}0\\
\frac{5\pi_{1}(1+\alpha)}{1+\alpha\pi_{1}}\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Substituting the class prevalence parameters <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}=0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}=0.99</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}=0.01</annotation></semantics></math> into the expression simplifies the coordinates to:</p>
<table id="S4.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{w}=\begin{pmatrix}0\\
\frac{0.05(1+\alpha)}{1+0.01\alpha}\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{w}=\begin{pmatrix}0\\
\frac{0.05(1+\alpha)}{1+0.01\alpha}\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The asymptotic weighted raw second-moment matrix is diagonal due to the alignment of the component axes, given by <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{w,\text{raw}}=\frac{\pi_{0}\mathbb{E}[XX^{\top}\mid Y=0]+\pi_{1}(1+\alpha)\mathbb{E}[XX^{\top}\mid Y=1]}{1+\alpha\pi_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>raw</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{w,\text{raw}}=\frac{\pi_{0}\mathbb{E}[XX^{\top}\mid Y=0]+\pi_{1}(1+\alpha)\mathbb{E}[XX^{\top}\mid Y=1]}{1+\alpha\pi_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The centered asymptotic weighted covariance matrix <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{w}=\Sigma_{w,\text{raw}}-\mu_{w}\mu_{w}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>raw</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{w}=\Sigma_{w,\text{raw}}-\mu_{w}\mu_{w}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> preserves this diagonal layout <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{w}=\operatorname{diag}(\Sigma_{w,11},\,\Sigma_{w,22})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>22</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{w}=\operatorname{diag}(\Sigma_{w,11},\,\Sigma_{w,22})</annotation></semantics></math>, where:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{w,11}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{w,11}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{99.01+0.01\alpha}{1+0.01\alpha}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>99.01</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{99.01+0.01\alpha}{1+0.01\alpha},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{w,22}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>22</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{w,22}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1.241+0.251\alpha}{1+0.01\alpha}-\frac{0.0025(1+\alpha)^{2}}{(1+0.01\alpha)^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.241</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.251</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.0025</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1.241+0.251\alpha}{1+0.01\alpha}-\frac{0.0025(1+\alpha)^{2}}{(1+0.01\alpha)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For TP-PCA to rotate away from the horizontal axis and successfully capture the discriminative vertical direction, the vertical component must strictly dominate the horizontal component, requiring the spectral inequality <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{w,22}&gt;\Sigma_{w,11}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>22</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{w,22}&gt;\Sigma_{w,11}</annotation></semantics></math>. Equating the common denominator systems yields:</p>
<table id="S4.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1.241+0.251\alpha}{1+0.01\alpha}-\frac{0.0025(1+\alpha)^{2}}{(1+0.01\alpha)^{2}}&gt;\frac{99.01+0.01\alpha}{1+0.01\alpha}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.241</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.251</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.0025</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>99.01</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1.241+0.251\alpha}{1+0.01\alpha}-\frac{0.0025(1+\alpha)^{2}}{(1+0.01\alpha)^{2}}&gt;\frac{99.01+0.01\alpha}{1+0.01\alpha}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">No matter how aggressively the user inflates the sample weights of the rare class, the subtractive mean shift <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{w}\mu_{w}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{w}\mu_{w}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> induced by the asymmetrical centering penalty scales at a rate that permanently suppresses the vertical variance relative to the horizontal component. TP-PCA is trapped at <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}=0^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}=0^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> for this distribution, yielding a fixed <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.99</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.99</annotation></semantics></math>-expectile decision tail risk of:</p>
<table id="S4.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{0.99}(L_{\text{TP-PCA}})=50.0000." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0.99</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>TP-PCA</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>50.0000</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{0.99}(L_{\text{TP-PCA}})=50.0000.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">This exact derivation uncovers a fundamental hidden vulnerability of supervised sample-weighting heuristics: without coordinating the centering mechanics alongside task-specific boundaries, mechanical inflation remains completely blind to tail risk.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">3. exPCA.
exPCA optimizes the unsupervised <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-expectile of the geometric reconstruction error distribution. Because the global variance is heavily concentrated along <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the reconstruction error function acts as a strong regularizer. Solving the implicit system coupled to Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Weighted Covariance Characterization). ‣ II-E Risk-Aware Unsupervised Dimensionality Reduction: exPCA ‣ II Problem Formulation ‣ The Risk Shadow of Principal Component Analysis: When 99.9999% Variance Preservation Causes Catastrophic Decision Errors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> isolates the optimal angle near the horizontal axis, rotating it only slightly to <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{exPCA}}\approx 10^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>exPCA</mtext></msub><mo>≈</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{exPCA}}\approx 10^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>. Due to the massive overlap of the projected distributions, the system suffers from a high False Negative rate (<math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 0.20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 0.20</annotation></semantics></math>), resulting in an expectile tail risk of:</p>
<table id="S4.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{0.99}(L_{\text{exPCA}})\approx 20.0000." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0.99</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>exPCA</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>20.0000</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{0.99}(L_{\text{exPCA}})\approx 20.0000.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">4. exp2PCA (Proposed)
We now evaluate the direct minimization of the cost expectile along the decision-theoretic optimal axis <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\text{exp2}}=(0,1)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mtext>exp2</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\text{exp2}}=(0,1)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, corresponding to <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}=90^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>90</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}=90^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>, without relying on any manual class-weight hyperparameters. The projection simplifies directly to <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding the conditional distributions <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\mid Y=0\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\mid Y=0\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\mid Y=1\sim\mathcal{N}(5,0.1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\mid Y=1\sim\mathcal{N}(5,0.1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">By setting an operational decision threshold at <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}=2.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}=2.5</annotation></semantics></math>, the directional error rates evaluate precisely to:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\text{False Positive})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>False Positive</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\text{False Positive})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\Phi(2.5)\approx 0.00621," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.00621</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\Phi(2.5)\approx 0.00621,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\text{False Negative})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>False Negative</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\text{False Negative})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Phi\left(\frac{2.5-5}{\sqrt{0.1}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2.5</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><msqrt><mn>0.1</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Phi\left(\frac{2.5-5}{\sqrt{0.1}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Phi(-7.90569)\approx 1.33\times 10^{-15}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>7.90569</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1.33</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Phi(-7.90569)\approx 1.33\times 10^{-15}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">Because the False Negative rate is driven to numerical zero, the high-cost penalty <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FN}=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FN}=100</annotation></semantics></math> is completely avoided. The decision loss distribution behaves as a scaled Bernoulli random variable, taking the value <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FP}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FP}=1</annotation></semantics></math> with an exact global probability of <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.99\times 0.00621=0.00615" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.99</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>0.00621</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.00615</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.99\times 0.00621=0.00615</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> with a complementary probability of <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-p=0.99385" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.99385</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-p=0.99385</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate the exact <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-expectile risk <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}=e_{0.99}(L_{\text{exp2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0.99</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>exp2</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}=e_{0.99}(L_{\text{exp2}})</annotation></semantics></math>, we execute the first-order optimization condition for a two-point distribution where <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;t^{*}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;t^{*}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\tau)(0-t^{*})(1-p)+\tau(1-t^{*})p=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\tau)(0-t^{*})(1-p)+\tau(1-t^{*})p=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p9.2" class="ltx_p">Substituting our exact parameters <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.99</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.00615" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.00615</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.00615</annotation></semantics></math> yields
directly to the hyperparameter-free optimal tail risk:</p>
<table id="S4.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{0.99}(L_{\text{exp2}})=\frac{\tau p}{(1-\tau)(1-p)+\tau p}=0.3799." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0.99</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>exp2</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3799</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{0.99}(L_{\text{exp2}})=\frac{\tau p}{(1-\tau)(1-p)+\tau p}=0.3799.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">By actively aligning the projection space with task-specific penalties rather than geometric summaries or heuristic sample weights, exp2PCA compresses the tail risk from <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50.0000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50.0000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50.0000</annotation></semantics></math> down to <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.3799" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.3799</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.3799</annotation></semantics></math>, eliminating the need for hyperparameter search over <math id="S4.SS2.SSSx1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">IV-C</span> </span><span id="S4.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Example 2: Discrete Distribution with an Isolated Target Point</span></h3>

<section id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Data Distribution.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a discrete probability space where the random vector <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=(x_{1},x_{2})^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=(x_{1},x_{2})^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is concentrated entirely on three point masses:</p>
<table id="S4.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\begin{cases}(10,0)^{\top}&amp;\text{with probability }0.49,\quad Y=0,\\
(-10,0)^{\top}&amp;\text{with probability }0.49,\quad Y=0,\\
(0,1)^{\top}&amp;\text{with probability }0.02,\quad Y=1.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>with probability </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0.49</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>with probability </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0.49</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>with probability </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\begin{cases}(10,0)^{\top}&amp;\text{with probability }0.49,\quad Y=0,\\
(-10,0)^{\top}&amp;\text{with probability }0.49,\quad Y=0,\\
(0,1)^{\top}&amp;\text{with probability }0.02,\quad Y=1.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The global mean vector is <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[X]=0.49\begin{pmatrix}10\\
0\end{pmatrix}+0.49\begin{pmatrix}-10\\
0\end{pmatrix}+0.02\begin{pmatrix}0\\
1\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}0\\
0.02\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.49</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>10</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.49</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0.02</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[X]=0.49\begin{pmatrix}10\\
0\end{pmatrix}+0.49\begin{pmatrix}-10\\
0\end{pmatrix}+0.02\begin{pmatrix}0\\
1\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}0\\
0.02\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>. The uncentered raw second-moment matrix is diagonal: <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[XX^{\top}]=0.49\begin{pmatrix}100&amp;0\\
0&amp;0\end{pmatrix}+0.49\begin{pmatrix}100&amp;0\\
0&amp;0\end{pmatrix}+0.02\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}98&amp;0\\
0&amp;0.02\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.49</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>100</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.49</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>100</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>98</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0.02</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[XX^{\top}]=0.49\begin{pmatrix}100&amp;0\\
0&amp;0\end{pmatrix}+0.49\begin{pmatrix}100&amp;0\\
0&amp;0\end{pmatrix}+0.02\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}98&amp;0\\
0&amp;0.02\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Subtracting the outer product of the mean yields the exact centered global covariance matrix:</p>
<table id="S4.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\mathbb{E}[XX^{\top}]-\mathbb{E}[X]\mathbb{E}[X]^{\top}=\begin{pmatrix}98&amp;0\\
0&amp;0.0196\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>98</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0.0196</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\mathbb{E}[XX^{\top}]-\mathbb{E}[X]\mathbb{E}[X]^{\top}=\begin{pmatrix}98&amp;0\\
0&amp;0.0196\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The operational constants are configured with <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FN}=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FN}=100</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FP}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FP}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and the tail risk metric is evaluated at <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.99</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Standard PCA and exPCA Failure.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is diagonal with a clear spectral gap (<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}=98\gg\lambda_{2}=0.0196" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>98</mn><mo>≫</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0196</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}=98\gg\lambda_{2}=0.0196</annotation></semantics></math>), standard PCA isolates the dominant horizontal direction <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\text{PCA}}=(1,0)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\text{PCA}}=(1,0)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}=0^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}=0^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>). Similarly, for exPCA, any deviation of <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> away from <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> projects the immense coordinate spread of the majority points (<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 10</annotation></semantics></math>) into the reconstruction error function <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{u}(X)=(10\sin\theta)^{2}=100\sin^{2}\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{u}(X)=(10\sin\theta)^{2}=100\sin^{2}\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. To minimize the upper tail of this geometric distortion, the first-order condition forces <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{exPCA}}=0^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>exPCA</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{exPCA}}=0^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, both unsupervised frameworks collapse the data onto the horizontal line <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under this projection, the majority class maps to <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 10</annotation></semantics></math>, while the rare target point maps directly to <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Because the target point is embedded in the middle of the majority components, no scalar threshold can isolate it. The optimal operational classifier is forced to select the constant majority prediction <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(z)\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(z)\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This results in a loss distribution <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> that takes the value <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FN}=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FN}=100</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}=0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}=0.02</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}=0.98" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.98</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}=0.98</annotation></semantics></math>. To find the exact <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-expectile risk <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=e_{0.99}(L_{\text{PCA}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0.99</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=e_{0.99}(L_{\text{PCA}})</annotation></semantics></math>, we execute the first-order stationarity condition for <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;t&lt;100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;t&lt;100</annotation></semantics></math>,
which simplifies to the precise risk value:</p>
<table id="S4.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{0.99}(L_{\text{PCA}})=e_{0.99}(L_{\text{exPCA}})\approx 66.8919." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0.99</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>PCA</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0.99</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>exPCA</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>66.8919</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{0.99}(L_{\text{PCA}})=e_{0.99}(L_{\text{exPCA}})\approx 66.8919.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Tail-Preserving PCA (TP-PCA) Evaluation.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">TP-PCA scales the rare-class components using the supervised weight <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w_{i}=1+\alpha\mathbf{1}_{\{Y_{i}=1\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}=1+\alpha\mathbf{1}_{\{Y_{i}=1\}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Asymptotically, the weighted mean vector tracks to <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{w}=\begin{pmatrix}0\\
\frac{0.02(1+\alpha)}{0.98+0.02(1+\alpha)}\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}0\\
\frac{0.02+0.02\alpha}{1+0.02\alpha}\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0.98</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{w}=\begin{pmatrix}0\\
\frac{0.02(1+\alpha)}{0.98+0.02(1+\alpha)}\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}0\\
\frac{0.02+0.02\alpha}{1+0.02\alpha}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>. The elements of the diagonal weighted covariance matrix <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> evaluate exactly to:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{w,11}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{w,11}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{96.04}{1+0.02\alpha}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>96.04</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{96.04}{1+0.02\alpha},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{w,22}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>22</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{w,22}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{0.02+0.02\alpha}{1+0.02\alpha}-\frac{0.0004(1+\alpha)^{2}}{(1+0.02\alpha)^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.0004</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{0.02+0.02\alpha}{1+0.02\alpha}-\frac{0.0004(1+\alpha)^{2}}{(1+0.02\alpha)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">To flip the principal component toward the discriminative vertical axis, the hyperparameter must satisfy <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{w,22}&gt;\Sigma_{w,11}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>22</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{w,22}&gt;\Sigma_{w,11}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Expanding and collecting the polynomial terms forms the following condition:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-1.9012\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1.9012</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-1.9012\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;96.0204." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>96.0204</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;96.0204.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Solving for the inflation factor reveals that the inequality holds only if <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;-50.505" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>50.505</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;-50.505</annotation></semantics></math>. Because the Stiefel hyperparameter is bounded by definition within the positive real domain (<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>), **there is no valid weighting factor that can rescue TP-PCA**. The centering penalty dominates the second-moment allocation, leaving TP-PCA trapped at <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}=0^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}=0^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> with a collapsed tail risk of <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="66.8919" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>66.8919</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">66.8919</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">exp2PCA Recovery.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Exp2PCA directly targets the optimization of the cost functional, choosing the vertical axis <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\text{exp2}}=(0,1)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mtext>exp2</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\text{exp2}}=(0,1)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}=90^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>90</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}=90^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>). The projection maps the coordinates onto the vertical line <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under this mapping, the majority points collapse safely to <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=0</annotation></semantics></math>, while the rare target point maps directly to <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By selecting a decision boundary threshold at <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> via the operational classifier <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h(z)=\mathbf{1}_{\{z&gt;0.5\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(z)=\mathbf{1}_{\{z&gt;0.5\}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the classes separate with a clean structural margin. The classification error rate drops to exactly zero for both false positives and false negatives across all support spaces. The downstream loss distribution collapses to a single delta mass centered at zero (<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(L=0)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(L=0)=1</annotation></semantics></math>). The direct minimization framework eliminates the decision penalty entirely from the upper tail:</p>
<table id="S4.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{0.99}(L_{\text{exp2}})=0.0000." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0.99</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>exp2</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0000</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{0.99}(L_{\text{exp2}})=0.0000.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This benchmark confirms that while standard unsupervised variance-maximization pipelines and supervised sample-weighting schemes remain mathematically blind to target structures, exp2PCA completely eliminates the operational tail risk.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Summary of Empirical Performance and Benchmarks</h4>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="TABLE II ‣ Summary of Empirical Performance and Benchmarks ‣ IV-C Example 2: Discrete Distribution with an Isolated Target Point ‣ IV Explicit Synthetic Benchmarks (2D, 𝑟=1) ‣ The Risk Shadow of Principal Component Analysis: When 99.9999% Variance Preservation Causes Catastrophic Decision Errors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">II</span></a> provides a comprehensive analytical comparison of the downstream decision tail risk across all four dimensionality reduction paradigms. The empirical configurations confirm that standard geometric formulations remain severely limited when critical classification boundaries align with minor principal components.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSSx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By avoiding indirect geometric proxies (such as global variance or reconstruction errors) and steering clear of uncoordinated sample-weighting heuristics, <span id="S4.SS3.SSSx1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">exp2PCA</span> directly optimizes the decision-theoretic risk functional. This strategic alignment compresses the operational <math id="S4.SS3.SSSx1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-expectile tail risk to near-zero levels across both continuous and discrete settings.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE II: </span><math id="S4.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-Expectile Misclassification Risk (<math id="S4.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{0.99}(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0.99</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{0.99}(L)</annotation></semantics></math>)</figcaption>
<table id="S4.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dataset Paradigm</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PCA Risk</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TP-PCA Risk</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">exPCA Risk</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">exp2PCA Risk</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T2.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Example 1: Gaussian Mixture</th>
