<td id="S5.T3.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="S5.T3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.840\pm 0.050" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.840</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.050</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.840\pm 0.050</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="S5.T3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.110\pm 0.010" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.110</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.010</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.110\pm 0.010</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.6.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="S5.T3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0.002\pm 0.001}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">0.002</mn><mo>±</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0.002\pm 0.001}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The empirical trajectories summarized in Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="TABLE III ‣ V-A Synthetic Benchmark Optimization Profiles ‣ V Empirical Validation ‣ The Risk Shadow of Principal Component Analysis: When 99.9999% Variance Preservation Causes Catastrophic Decision Errors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III</span></a> confirm our structural theorems. Standard PCA captures the dominant global variance (<math id="S5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="95.2\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>95.2</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95.2\%</annotation></semantics></math>), but exhibits complete information erasure regarding the target variable, resulting in a near-random Area Under the ROC Curve (AUC = <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.51" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.51</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.51</annotation></semantics></math>) and a severe expectile risk (<math id="S5.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{0.99}=0.870" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mn>0.99</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.870</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{0.99}=0.870</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Supervised class-weighting (TP-PCA) under a standard prevalence matching parameter (<math id="S5.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=99</annotation></semantics></math>) fails to rotate the principal subspace away from the background noise matrix due to the uncoordinated centering penalty. This yields a collapsed AUC of <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.53" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.53</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.53</annotation></semantics></math>.
exPCA begins capturing rare-event dynamics by penalizing geometric tail outliers, achieving an AUC of <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.94" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.94</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.94</annotation></semantics></math>. exp2PCA explicitly trades off global variance representation (<math id="S5.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="41.6\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>41.6</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">41.6\%</annotation></semantics></math>) to directly minimize downstream operational cost, maximizing the captured mutual information (<math id="S5.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.890" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.890</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.890</annotation></semantics></math> nats) and compressing the final decision-theoretic tail risk to <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0.002}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">0.002</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0.002}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">V-B</span> </span><span id="S5.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Real-World Benchmarks across High-Stakes Application Domains</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate the operational robustness of the frameworks under real-world asymmetric constraints, we test performance across ten public benchmarking configurations. For each configuration, the risk environment is evaluated under a strict tail parameter <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.995" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.995</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.995</annotation></semantics></math>. The penalty parameters are scaled asymmetrically, setting the False Negative cost <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FN}=100\times C_{FP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FN}=100\times C_{FP}</annotation></semantics></math> to simulate high-stakes default, intrusion, or diagnostic omission risks. Downstream classification across all feature extraction strategies is executed via a standardized, cross-validated linear classifier.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">V-B</span>1 </span>Credit Card Fraud Detection</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Data Infrastructure <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite>:</span> 284,807 transactions with an extreme class imbalance profile consisting of 492 fraudulent instances (<math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{rare}}=0.17\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>rare</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.17</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{rare}}=0.17\%</annotation></semantics></math>). Features comprise 30 numerical attributes.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Decision Asymmetry:</span> Missed fraudulent actions incur transaction re-crediting and chargeback processing fees (<math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FN}=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FN}=100</annotation></semantics></math>), whereas False Positives generate temporary hold notifications (<math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FP}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FP}=1</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Performance Optimization:</span> Standard PCA components remain completely bound to majority-class nominal transaction variances, limiting classification performance to an AUC of <math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.62" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.62</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.62</annotation></semantics></math>. exp2PCA successfully isolates the subtle coordinate combinations that capture structural fraud signatures, increasing the operational AUC to <math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0.91}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">0.91</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0.91}</annotation></semantics></math> while driving down the tail risk from <math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.92" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.92</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.92</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0.15}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">0.15</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0.15}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S5.SS2.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">V-B</span>2 </span>Life Insurance Fraud Detection</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S5.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Data Infrastructure <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>]</cite>:</span> 4,000 insurance applications tracking 83 distinct attributes detailing demographics, financial history, and medical records, displaying a baseline fraud prevalence of <math id="S5.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim 15\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim 15\%</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Decision Asymmetry:</span> Granting a policy to an application containing fraudulent omissions risks an unhedged catastrophic payout (<math id="S5.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FN}=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FN}=100</annotation></semantics></math>), while False Positives only add a standard manual administrative audit (<math id="S5.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FP}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FP}=1</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Performance Optimization:</span> Standard unsupervised compression structures blend the application features across background economic variances. exp2PCA preserves the specialized behavioral anomalies along minor components, elevating the target class recall and reducing the tail risk metric by a factor of 4.2.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S5.SS2.SSS3.6" class="ltx_text">V-B</span>3 </span>Vehicle Insurance Claim Fraud Analysis</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S5.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Data Infrastructure <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite>:</span> 15,420 insurance claims across 33 technical features tracking vehicle attributes, claimant demographics, and accident descriptions, with a positive fraud rate of <math id="S5.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim 6\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim 6\%</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Decision Asymmetry:</span> Failing to catch a staged or inflated claim drains reserves directly (<math id="S5.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FN}=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FN}=100</annotation></semantics></math>), whereas an investigative false alarm generates a minor administrative review cost (<math id="S5.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FP}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FP}=1</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Performance Optimization:</span> Unsupervised frameworks focus on nominal policy variations. exp2PCA extracts the specific coordinate vectors that indicate deceptive claiming patterns, mitigating tail risk without requiring synthetic oversampling or over-parameterization.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S5.SS2.SSS4.6" class="ltx_text">V-B</span>4 </span>Multivariate Time-Series Paper Break Prediction</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S5.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Data Infrastructure <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>, <a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite>:</span> 18,398 industrial sensor records across 61 continuous multivariate process streams, containing 124 positive paper break events (<math id="S5.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{rare}}=0.67\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>rare</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.67</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{rare}}=0.67\%</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Decision Asymmetry:</span> An unpredicted sheet break triggers immediate mechanical downtime, costing thousands of dollars per hour (<math id="S5.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FN}=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FN}=100</annotation></semantics></math>), while a false warning triggers only a brief visual sensor inspection (<math id="S5.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FP}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FP}=1</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Performance Optimization:</span> Standard PCA maps components exclusively to high-energy thermodynamic fluctuations. exp2PCA isolates the low-amplitude acoustic and rotational sensor harmonics that serve as precursors to sheet failure, allowing reliable early fault prediction.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S5.SS2.SSS5.6" class="ltx_text">V-B</span>5 </span>Network Intrusion Detection (Ultra-Rare Attack Vectors)</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S5.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Data Infrastructure <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">57</a>]</cite>:</span> 2.8 million network packet flows tracking 80 high-dimensional network attributes. The target vectors comprise ultra-rare malicious attack variants (e.g., Heartbleed: 11 instances; Infiltration: 36 instances).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Decision Asymmetry:</span> Undetected perimeter breaches threaten data exfiltration and persistent network compromise (<math id="S5.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FN}=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FN}=100</annotation></semantics></math>), while False Positives cause minor internal traffic routing overhead (<math id="S5.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FP}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FP}=1</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Performance Optimization:</span> Unsupervised projections are dominated by nominal high-volume data packet trends. exp2PCA isolates low-energy attack profiles from background noise, boosting rare attack classification AUC to <math id="S5.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0.89}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">0.89</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0.89}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS6" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S5.SS2.SSS6.6" class="ltx_text">V-B</span>6 </span>Chest X-Ray Long-Tailed Pathology Classification</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S5.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Data Infrastructure <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite>:</span> 145,000 clinical medical chest radiographs mapped through deep convolutional feature extractors, presenting a severely skewed long-tailed distribution of rare thoracic pathologies.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Decision Asymmetry:</span> Diagnostic omission of a rare, progressive pulmonary condition risks irreversible patient deterioration (<math id="S5.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FN}=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FN}=100</annotation></semantics></math>), whereas a False Positive triggers a secondary diagnostic scan (<math id="S5.I6.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FP}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FP}=1</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I6.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Performance Optimization:</span> Standard embedding PCA captures general structural features (lung volume, bone orientation). By optimizing the representation directly against asymmetric clinical cost matrices, exp2PCA increases the mean Average Precision (mAP) on the rare pathological long-tail from <math id="S5.I6.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.53" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.53</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.53</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.I6.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0.62}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">0.62</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0.62}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS7" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S5.SS2.SSS7.6" class="ltx_text">V-B</span>7 </span>Bank Marketing Optimization for Term Deposit Subscription</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S5.I7" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I7.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Data Infrastructure <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>]</cite>:</span> 45,211 direct marketing interactions tracking 16 client demographic and historic behavioral attributes, exhibiting an asymmetric conversion rate of <math id="S5.I7.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11.3\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>11.3</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11.3\%</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I7.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Decision Asymmetry:</span> Misclassifying an open customer as non-subscribing squanders the client’s long-term lifetime value (<math id="S5.I7.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FN}=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FN}=100</annotation></semantics></math>), while a False Positive consumes only the minor marginal cost of an outbound call (<math id="S5.I7.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FP}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FP}=1</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I7.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Performance Optimization:</span> By shifting the feature compression step toward direct tail-risk targets, exp2PCA uncovers subtle financial indicators on minor components, yielding an absolute AUC improvement of <math id="S5.I7.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0.12}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">0.12</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0.12}</annotation></semantics></math> over standard PCA projections.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS8" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S5.SS2.SSS8.6" class="ltx_text">V-B</span>8 </span>Telco Customer Churn Minimization</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S5.I8" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I8.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Data Infrastructure <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>]</cite>:</span> 7,043 subscriber profiles across 20 attributes tracking demographics, account billing metrics, and network utilization logs, exhibiting a churn rate of <math id="S5.I8.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="26.5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>26.5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">26.5\%</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I8.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Decision Asymmetry:</span> Failing to flag a churning user breaks a recurring subscription revenue stream (<math id="S5.I8.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FN}=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FN}=100</annotation></semantics></math>), while a False Positive triggers a minor retention discount offer (<math id="S5.I8.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FP}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FP}=1</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I8.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I8.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I8.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I8.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Performance Optimization:</span> Standard PCA isolates macro-demographic variance. exp2PCA maps representations around structural behavioral anomalies, identifying slipping subscribers on low-variance channels and cutting operational tail risk by over half.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS9" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S5.SS2.SSS9.6" class="ltx_text">V-B</span>9 </span>Consumer Loan Default Risk Modeling</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S5.I9" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I9.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I9.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I9.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I9.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Data Infrastructure <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>]</cite>:</span> 2.2 million credit lines tracking over 100 borrower financial risk metrics, with a baseline default rate of <math id="S5.I9.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;5\%</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I9.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I9.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I9.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I9.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Decision Asymmetry:</span> Approving a defaulting borrower risks losing the entire outstanding loan principal (<math id="S5.I9.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FN}=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FN}=100</annotation></semantics></math>), while rejecting a creditworthy applicant forfeits only the marginal interest yield (<math id="S5.I9.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FP}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FP}=1</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I9.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I9.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I9.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I9.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Performance Optimization:</span> Traditional PCA achieves a baseline AUC of <math id="S5.I9.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.71" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.71</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.71</annotation></semantics></math>. By realigning the projection step with the underlying cost matrix, exp2PCA raises the operational default detection AUC to <math id="S5.I9.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0.84}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">0.84</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0.84}</annotation></semantics></math> by retaining low-variance credit markers.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS10" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S5.SS2.SSS10.6" class="ltx_text">V-B</span>10 </span>Automated PCB Defect Detection in High-Precision Manufacturing</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S5.I10" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I10.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I10.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I10.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I10.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Data Infrastructure <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>]</cite>:</span> 100,000 industrial visual manufacturing logs tracking surface integrity, with an underlying component defect rate of <math id="S5.I10.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim 2\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim 2\%</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I10.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I10.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I10.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I10.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Decision Asymmetry:</span> Allowing a defective board to pass inspection breaks downstream systems and risks liability claims (<math id="S5.I10.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FN}=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FN}=100</annotation></semantics></math>), while a False Positive simply reroutes the board for automated re-testing (<math id="S5.I10.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{FP}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{FP}=1</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I10.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I10.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I10.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I10.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Performance Optimization:</span> Visual PCA captures macro-geometric structures (board layout, mask boundaries). exp2PCA successfully isolates microscopic trace breaks and solder anomalies on minor components, raising the empirical defect recall rate from <math id="S5.I10.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.55" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.55</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.55</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.I10.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0.92}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">0.92</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0.92}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE IV: </span>Downstream Comparative Performance Across Ten Public Real-World Benchmarks. Results list Area Under the ROC Curve (AUC) and the Asymmetric Tail Risk Metric (<math id="S5.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{0.995}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mn>0.995</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{0.995}</annotation></semantics></math>) under a 100:1 cost ratio constraint.</figcaption>
<table id="S5.T4.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T4.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T4.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_border_tt"></td>
<th id="S5.T4.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" colspan="2"><span id="S5.T4.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard PCA</span></th>
<th id="S5.T4.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" colspan="2"><span id="S5.T4.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TP-PCA</span></th>
<th id="S5.T4.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" colspan="2"><span id="S5.T4.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">exPCA</span></th>
<th id="S5.T4.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" colspan="2"><span id="S5.T4.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">exp2PCA</span> (Ours)</th></tr>
<tr id="S5.T4.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T4.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column"><span id="S5.T4.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Real-World Benchmark Dataset</span></th>
<th id="S5.T4.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T4.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AUC</span></th>
<th id="S5.T4.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{0.995}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mn>0.995</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{0.995}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S5.T4.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T4.2.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AUC</span></th>
<th id="S5.T4.2.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{0.995}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mn>0.995</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{0.995}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S5.T4.2.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T4.2.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AUC</span></th>
<th id="S5.T4.2.2.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{0.995}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mn>0.995</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{0.995}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S5.T4.2.2.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T4.2.2.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AUC</span></th>
<th id="S5.T4.2.2.9" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{0.995}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mn>0.995</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{0.995}</annotation></semantics></math></th></tr>
<tr id="S5.T4.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T4.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">1. Credit Card Fraud Detection</td>
<td id="S5.T4.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.62" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.62</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.62</annotation></semantics></math></td>
